{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting","id":1379651,"title":"Is V5 a NobleBright setting?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-08T23:21:13-07:00","id":1379651,"title":"Is V5 a NobleBright setting?","content":"I'm making my first V5 character and have been reading into the book and lore. The more I read, the more the setting seems like a NobleBright setting to me.<br /> <br /> While I have never played VTM until recently, I have been reading up on its lore over the years (mostly the wiki) and did play a little of VTMB. All this time there seems to be a doom and gloom feel to the world setting of VTM. The Kindred faces the final nights (end of the world). While kine are secretly being controlled by various forces including vamps, which are in control of various governments, organizations etc.<br /> <br /> Basically the whole setting used to have this Grimdark feel to it.<br /> <br /> Reading the V5 books, it feels very hopeful and good for humanity. Yes there are still vamps, but they have lost most of the elders, many of their power structures are destroyed or damaged. And now humans know and actively able to hunt vamps. Vamps that are not even as strong any more, since plenty of the older, more powerful ones have been sucked away to some fight.<br /> <br /> The 2nd inquisition seems to know what they see doing and pretty much cataloged most of what vamps can do (implied by the report info on each discipline). It's just a matter of time before they shot or bomb every vamp to death. With technology on their side.<br /> <br /> So while it's like the end for vamps and to be honest the lore now reads more like &quot;Vampire the Extinction&quot;. It's a whole lot of win for humanity. It's just a matter of time before even the darkest places still controlled by vamps get nuked by the 2nd inquisition.<br /> <br /> So is the setting of V5, as a whole, considered NobleBright?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26067-wingstorm","name":"Wingstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T23:48:08-07:00","id":1379663,"title":"","content":"I mean it shouldn't be, Vampires are parasites and benefit by harming others secretly. Maybe its noblebright for Humanity because they may win.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T23:51:24-07:00","id":1379666,"title":"","content":"Well, I mean. Theoretically you should be looking at this from the point of view of a vampire, in which case things haven't been <i>worse </i>in a long time. <br /> <br /> As for it being better for humanity, well, this is still the world of darkness, where things suck for everyone and the apocalypse is just around the corner. Even if all the vampires get killed, maybe humans still get nommed by antediluvians and such come Gehenna.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25545-jollycooperative","name":"jollycooperative","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T23:58:52-07:00","id":1379672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jollycooperative</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379666#post1379666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I mean. Theoretically you should be looking at this from the point of view of a vampire, in which case things haven't been <i>worse </i>in a long time.<br /> <br /> As for it being better for humanity, well, this is still the world of darkness, where things suck for everyone and the apocalypse is just around the corner. Even if all the vampires get killed, maybe humans still get nommed by antediluvians and such come Gehenna.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean the Apocalyspe seemed much more around the Corner at the Turning of the New Millenium. Is the Red Star still in the sky?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T00:22:17-07:00","id":1379684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wingstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting#post1379651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm making my first V5 character and have been reading into the book and lore. The more I read, the more the setting seems like a NobleBright setting to me.<br /> <br /> While I have never played VTM until recently, I have been reading up on its lore over the years (mostly the wiki) and did play a little of VTMB. All this time there seems to be a doom and gloom feel to the world setting of VTM. The Kindred faces the final nights (end of the world). While kine are secretly being controlled by various forces including vamps, which are in control of various governments, organizations etc.<br /> <br /> Basically the whole setting used to have this Grimdark feel to it.<br /> <br /> Reading the V5 books, it feels very hopeful and good for humanity. Yes there are still vamps, but they have lost most of the elders, many of their power structures are destroyed or damaged. And now humans know and actively able to hunt vamps. Vamps that are not even as strong any more, since plenty of the older, more powerful ones have been sucked away to some fight.<br /> <br /> The 2nd inquisition seems to know what they see doing and pretty much cataloged most of what vamps can do (implied by the report info on each discipline). It's just a matter of time before they shot or bomb every vamp to death. With technology on their side.<br /> <br /> So while it's like the end for vamps and to be honest the lore now reads more like &quot;Vampire the Extinction&quot;. It's a whole lot of win for humanity. It's just a matter of time before even the darkest places still controlled by vamps get nuked by the 2nd inquisition.<br /> <br /> So is the setting of V5, as a whole, considered NobleBright?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Second Inquisition is seemingly based on the Nazis.<br /> <br /> So....<br /> <br /> No?<br /> <br /> Prison camps, medical experimentation, fascist subversion of governents as well as the people, and sadistic psychopaths getting off on hunting the most dangerous game.<br /> <br /> If they win they will make the world even worse because they're the same thing that makes vampires evil: they're humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-09-2020, 03:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T00:26:04-07:00","id":1379686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379672#post1379672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean the Apocalyspe seemed much more around the Corner at the Turning of the New Millenium. Is the Red Star still in the sky?</div> </div> </div> </div>For those with the eyes to see it, yes. Also bear in mind that the Week of Nightmares did happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T00:28:54-07:00","id":1379687,"title":"","content":"Once the Second Inquisition has eliminated the weaker vampires, then the antediluvians will reign unopposed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T00:48:22-07:00","id":1379691,"title":"","content":"Its laughable to think the thousand times over host of proven pawns will in any way be an obstacle to the Antes rather then a Tool. I mean baring some prophetic Last Daughter of Eve McGuffin.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379686#post1379686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For those with the eyes to see it, yes. Also bear in mind that the Week of Nightmares did happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>See I was confused on what was retconned and what wasn't especially after V20 kind of had its own continuity .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T01:16:40-07:00","id":1379707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379691#post1379691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its laughable to think the thousand times over host of proven pawns will in any way be an obstacle to the Antes rather then a Tool. I mean baring some prophetic Last Daughter of Eve McGuffin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on how powerful you see the Antes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T03:31:17-07:00","id":1379720,"title":"","content":"no since the second inquisition is made of primarily of religious extremists and government agencies looking to increase their own power. there are no good guys in this conflict. on top of that while high gen kindred are definitely threatened by the inquisition low gen kindred like methusulas and antedeluvians are lovecraftian in their powerlevel on top of being conniving bastards known to disappear for eons. the inquisition ain't gonna destroy them and they're not gonna stop siring for whatever twisted plots they've got in mind.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25992-archderd","name":"archderd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T03:36:02-07:00","id":1379722,"title":"","content":"in previous editions, antideluvians rising and the approach of gehenna is caused by the increased number of vampiric deaths<br /> (especially in Revised where high gen unlife expectancy was a joke)<br /> <br /> so, the Inquisition is actually speeding up the appocalypse, not slowing it down (though some antideluvians may be weaker as a result, due to having less progeny to devour)<br /> <br /> the world is actually worse in v5, since back then, even if all was lost, vampires were still acting as if there was still time (because there was no sign that it was over),<br /> but now, the 'all is lost' is right in front of you, you can only act as if...all is lost<br /> <br /> now, we don't know what fate is reserved for humans, because in previous editions, regular vampires have no more influence on the world since their fall during the dark ages,<br /> only methuselah and antideluvian can truly have any effect,<br /> <br /> and we have yet to see what MtA and WtA has in store for them,<br /> iirc, in MtA, there were possible good endings for humanity","signa