on-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T12:40:07-07:00","id":1379832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379830#post1379830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sorry but everytime you trash the Anarchs, I can't read your posts. I blame frenzy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but i'm honestly curious, what on earth makes you think things have gotten darker? It's the polar opposite of the theme i got. Even the godawful hunger is less mature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T12:48:10-07:00","id":1379833,"title":"","content":"It's that sense of naivette and innocence of the first edition they are trying to reenact now what probably gives the noblebright feel. Make it more personal than horror. I, for one,wait for the expansion of the world setting with which more good old grimdark will be added.<br /> <br /> If they really drop it and stay with VtR-like nonsense like 'local mysterious' stuff only and you as a ST or a player have no tools/rules/lore to go bigger/wider/darker, it'll be a death sentence for the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T12:53:09-07:00","id":1379834,"title":"","content":"- Technocracy is nazi. Second Inquisition is nazi. Sabbat is nazi. You can't play them or you become one.<br /> - Who do I play then?<br /> - Not a nazi.<br /> - And who is that?<br /> - Why.. Anarchs, of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","user":"Val_Nir","date":". 04-09-2020, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T13:16:45-07:00","id":1379856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379834#post1379834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Technocracy is nazi. Second Inquisition is nazi. Sabbat is nazi. You can't play them or you become one.<br /> - Who do I play then?<br /> - Not a nazi.<br /> - And who is that?<br /> - Why.. Anarchs, of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, all the bad guys are basically nazis in a different form. How original of the V5 writers, eh?<br /> <br /> Ironically, I remember a time when the Anarchs also had literal Nazis in their ranks. Gangs like the final Reich were once considered valid parts of the Anarch movement, even if most of the other Anarch groups despised them. But now of course, the face of the anarchs are people like Rudi the magic gay muslim vampire who is somehow still alive despite being outrageously offensive and dangerous to the vast majority of Camarilla Elders over 60 years of age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25604-nuclearsnake","name":"NuclearSnake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25604_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T13:31:50-07:00","id":1379864,"title":"","content":"<br /> The Darkest faction (sabbat) has disappeared. <br /> The Monopolistic organization (camarilla) has lost their monopoly. They've also been making lots of stupid mistakes. Most of their powerbase has left them, being pushed to the next group. <br /> The anti-oppressive vampires have gained a lot of ground and oh so many members<br /> The scary, independent, theocratic independent groups have liberalised and rebranded themselves. <br /> The Humans have risen up, abandoned the shackles of their corruption, and fight off the vampire menace, delivering their comeuppance. <br /> <br /> Seems like the nastier the group, the nastier the fate. The Better the group, the kinder the fate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T13:53:23-07:00","id":1379870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NuclearSnake</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379856#post1379856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, all the bad guys are basically nazis in a different form. How original of the V5 writers, eh?<br /> <br /> Ironically, I remember a time when the Anarchs also had literal Nazis in their ranks. Gangs like the final Reich were once considered valid parts of the Anarch movement, even if most of the other Anarch groups despised them. But now of course, the face of the anarchs are people like Rudi the magic gay muslim vampire who is somehow still alive despite being outrageously offensive and dangerous to the vast majority of Camarilla Elders over 60 years of age.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am totally fine with Rudi (except the magic part). But I am fine with stuff like Final Reich too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T14:17:06-07:00","id":1379875,"title":"","content":"Mostly it feels like they have moved towards making you the underdog no matter what you play. Even if you are Camarilla, you are still an underdog member of a group that has lost its most powerful members and is in constant danger from the Inquisition. You have no real option of playing The Man, just underdogs who might be slightly less underdog than other options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T14:19:47-07:00","id":1379876,"title":"","content":"Although I consider the setting more complex than before, I admit that weakening the Tower and the Sword and strengthening the Inquisition and the Anarchs, the mood of the game has changed. The vampires are may be no more in the Final Nights fighting in an ancient war that never ends, and may be they are not always pawns of elders and the fighting for freedoms is a major theme. But in V5 the focus is not only in the second inquisition, it is in the inner monster, in the decadence of humanity, in hunting and murder human beings for survive. Probably, this is the most psychological grimdark edition. In this edition the enemy is not the other sect or the elders, it is your own beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T14:29:27-07:00","id":1379879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justycar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379876#post1379876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although I consider the setting more complex than before, I admit that weakening the Tower and the Sword and strengthening the Inquisition and the Anarchs, the mood of the game has changed. The vampires are may be no more in the Final Nights fighting in an ancient war that never ends, and may be they are not always pawns of elders and the fighting for freedoms is a major theme. But in V5 the focus is not only in the second inquisition, it is in the inner monster, in the decadence of humanity, in hunting and murder human beings for survive. Probably, this is the most psychological grimdark edition. In this edition the enemy is not the other sect or the elders, it is your own beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe i could see this, if there was still Humanity.<br /> <br /> Now, though, morality has been utterly gutted. There's wishy washy tenets, touchstones, stains.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T15:23:57-07:00","id":1379897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jamiemalk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379879#post1379879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe i could see this, if there was still Humanity.<br /> <br /> Now, though, morality has been utterly gutted. There's wishy washy tenets, touchstones, stains.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, there's morality that reflects the groups morals and views as well as characters can actually have different views on morality without relying on a victorian era model for &quot;Good and right&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","name":"Necroticbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T15:36:59-07:00","id":1379900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necroticbinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379897#post1379897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, there's morality that reflects the groups morals and views as well as characters can actually have different views on morality without relying on a victorian era model for &quot;Good and right&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, awful idea, Path of Do Whatever I Want, coterie edition basically. Removes pretty much all of the personal horror.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T15:46:00-07:00","id":1379904,"title":"","content":"Clearly. Except the difference is actual paths are that from older editions while in the current edition of V5, you can you know, set the tone and theme of your game so your sins reflect that. Given that I've had groups tank humanity faster in V5 than previously, it's clearly always used as path of do whatever I want.<br /> <br /> The problem with your argument there is that if a group doesn't want to deal with humanity and have the path of whatever I was going to do anyways, the edition doesn't matter. The current edition gives the players and storyteller input on what SHOULD be worthy of losing humanity and better fits different views and outputs which paths so clearly wanted to do rather than actually being alien points of view.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","name":"Necroticbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T15:53:35-07:00","id":1379908,"title":"","content":"Is NobleBright a bad thing? I personally think Vampire should be like a grittier version of Twilight, or Vampire Diaries but not so over the top. But other people see it differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T15:55:02-07:00","id":1379909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necroticbinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379904#post1379904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The current edition gives the players and storyteller input on what SHOULD be worthy of losing humanity and better fits different views and outputs which paths so clearly wanted to do rather than actually being alien points of view.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Watering it down. Making it <i>less</i> about the inevitable decent, becoming a monster.<br /> <br /> Honestly, if your players are tanking path, that they picked the sins for, it sounds more like there's a bigger problem there. Path is harder to lose than ever before<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T16:08:32-07:00","id":1379915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379908#post1379908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is NobleBright a bad thing? I personally think Vampire should be like a grittier version of Twilight, or Vampire Diaries but not so over the top. But other people see it differently.</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely not a bad one as long as it continues the Vampire games' tradition of catering to all levels of 'gritty and dark'. Yours are grittier version of Twilight and Vampire Diaries, mine are with mood from Seven, Sicario, Apocalypse Now, Red State, Beast of no Nation and City of God. previous vampire editions especially the most successful one (Revised) provided mood, lore, and tools for both 'extremeties' and anything in between. V5 feels to be leaning heavily toward yours only.<br /> <br /> Again, that's how it feels for now. I hope for the best and eagerly look forward to their next books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T16:11:37-07:00","id":1379917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jamiemalk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379909#post1379909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes. Watering it down. Making it <i>less</i> about the inevitable decent, becoming a monster.<br /> <br /> Honestly, if your players are tanking path, that they picked the sins for, it sounds more like there's a bigger problem there. Path is harder to lose than ever before</div> </div> </div> </div>It's really not. Again, that is entirely about your group and how they are playing. In V5, you can actually wight out. In V20 and earlier editions. Excluding diablerie, you weren't going to unless you were trying to find new ways of committing atrocities. <br /> <hr /><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Absolutely not a bad one as long as it continues the Vampire games' tradition of catering to all levels of 'gritty and dark'. Yours are grittier version of Twilight and Vampire Diaries, mine are with mood from Seven, Sicario, Apocalypse Now, Red State, Beast of no Nation and City of God. previous vampire editions especially the most successful one (Revised) provided mood, lore, and tools for both 'extremeties' and anything in between. V5 feels to be leaning heavily toward yours only. </div> </div> </div>Because V5 has vampires being kidnapped and experimented on, the young still being abused and dying by the dozens. It seems like it's leaning pretty heavily in doing whatever you want. Care to provide an example of how it's failing to support the 'darker' parts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","name":"Necroticbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T16:16:56-07:00","id":1379919,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25988_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25988\" data-vbnamecard=\"25988\">Val_Nir</a> thanks. Your playing style is totally valid too.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m probably gonna pick up Fall of London soon. If you want I\u2019ll be happy to let you know what I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T16:35:03-07:00","id":1379929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necroticbinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379917#post1379917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's really not. Again, that is entirely about your group and how they are playing. In V5, you can actually wight out. In V20 and earlier editions. Excluding diablerie, you weren't going to unless you were trying to find new ways of committing atrocities.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd have to walk me through that, i've gone down to Humanity 0 without diablerie in V20, just by using dominate.<br /> <br /> Like, they're breaking tenets, which they agreed to, so often they're filling their humanity tracks up and having to take a humanity check, each session, and they're not learning from it? That sounds like a <i><u>very</u></i> deliberate attempt to wassail over multiple sessions, or you're hammering them far harder than Humanity ever was in previous editions...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T16:45:54-07:00","id":1379934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379919#post1379919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25988_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25988\" data-vbnamecard=\"25988\">Val_Nir</a> thanks. Your playing style is totally valid too.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m probably gonna pick up Fall of London soon. If you want I\u2019ll be happy to let you know what I think.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Absolutely. I really really love stories about secret societies and conspiracies springing from decades of scheming and maneuvering to just several nights of violence. and especially since it is - it was - an unassailable bastion of the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Hopefully we get a Fall of Mexico some day, too. The notes on it and the start of 4th Civil war in BJD are nothing short of amazing.<br /> Looking forward to know your opinion, most probably I'll get my copy too after hearing it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T16:52:22-07:00","id":1379938,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25988_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25988\" data-vbnamecard=\"25988\">Val_Nir</a> I like violence in my games. I just like hearts and romance too.<br /> <br /> Fall of Mexico would be awesome \ud83d\ude0a.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T16:54:13-07:00","id":1379940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jamiemalk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379929#post1379929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You'd have to walk me through that, i've gone down to Humanity 0 without diablerie in V20, just by using dominate.<br /> <br /> Like, they're breaking tenets, which they agreed to, so often they're filling their humanity tracks up and having to take a humanity check, each session, and they're not learning from it? That sounds like a <i><u>very</u></i> deliberate attempt to wassail over multiple sessions, or you're hammering them far harder than Humanity ever was in previous editions...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's like saying that someone violating humanity sins (Which are, in effective, 3-4 more tenets, unless you count convictions) is players doing something deliberately and not learning from it each session.<br /> <br /> To go down to Humanity 1 requires multiple mass murders, to get bbelow humanity 1 well. It requires as it states &quot;Utter perversion or heinous acts&quot;<br /> <br /> The easiest tenets to lose are humanist humanity on are humanist. &quot;Don't kill, don't enslave or torture and don't harm the innocent.&quot;. I'd say that characters can learn and still be forced into situations where they will have to kill, harm, or enslave people to protect the masquerade or what they value. This of course doesn't include the problems that can be forced on people based on what convictions they have and if those get violated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","name":"Necroticbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T16:58:52-07:00","id":1379942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jamiemalk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379832#post1379832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but i'm honestly curious, what on earth makes you think things have gotten darker? It's the polar opposite of the theme i got. Even the godawful hunger is less mature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Back in the original World of Darkness, there was a struggle between &quot;adult content&quot; vs. &quot;for our largely teenage audience of Goth kids and white suburbanites mildly rebelling against their parents that include considerable overlap.&quot; This isn't me making a supposition, it's the reason why Black Dog Games existed. Black Dog Games existed to be the more mature darker lineage and while some were complete fucking disasters (I own one of the few remaining copies of Eternal Hearts that hasn't been burned by sane men), others were dealing with the extreme dark themes and violence that was usually only alluded at.<br /> <br /> <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> 5E is a game that is marketed not at teenagers but at the now-thirty something original audience of the Nineties. The teenagers who have grown up. So was V20 for the most part but this has gone even more so. They've embraced dark topics, violence, and political subjects (sometimes to considerable disaster) while reaffirming the game's social content. It's all Black Dog now.<br /> <br /> So, yes, I feel V5 is a darker more mature take on the World of Darkness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T17:03:28-07:00","id":1379946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jamiemalk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379929#post1379929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, they're breaking tenets, which they agreed to, so often they're filling their humanity tracks up and having to take a humanity check, each session, and they're not learning from it? That sounds like a <i><u>very</u></i> deliberate attempt to wassail over multiple sessions, or you're hammering them far harder than Humanity ever was in previous editions...</div> </div> </div> </div>The <i>players</i> agree to the tenets, which define the theme and mood and tone of the game. Sure, you can choose tenets that your characters will never break\u2026but then what's the point? That just makes humanity meaningless.<br /> <br /> More often, in my experience, players and STs come up with tenets that will intentionally drive conflict in the game and require the characters to make difficult choices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T17:09:46-07:00","id":1379948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379772#post1379772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a world that is darker and more deadly than our just, but vampires seem like they're on their way to extinction is a NobleBright setting then I guess we're definitely living in one. I mean, we don't even have vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the vampires are on their way to extinction. This seems like it's meant to be nothing so much (or less) than a repeat of the Middle Ages. The Inquisition pressures vampires, the vampires war over age as well as generation, and then the two sides eventually agree to double down on the Masquerade while others decide to go wild instead. The big difference is that humans are wielding Uzis and drones rather than stakes.<br /> <br /> I am inclined to think the Second Inquisition will fail, though, because of internal corruption.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379772#post1379772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a world that is darker and more deadly than our just, but vampires seem like they're on their way to extinction is a NobleBright setting then I guess we're definitely living in one. I mean, we don't even have vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're Himmler and Goring Sabbat? Which is a statement I never thought I'd say.<br /> <br /> This is something that's just a house rule but generally, I think most vampires are sexually fluid past sixty. The blood is sex and all vampires derive sexual pleasure from the blood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is NobleBright a bad thing? I personally think Vampire should be like a grittier version of Twilight, or Vampire Diaries but not so over the top. But other people see it differently.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think vampire has no &quot;one true way.&quot; V:TM should be able to encompass Angel, Buffy, Forever Knight, Moonlight, The Vampire Chronicle, The Vampire Files, Dracula, Near Dark, Lost Boys, and yes the Vampire Diaries (which are darker than they seem). Games will vary at the table but the idea is you should be able to handle most kinds of vampires.<br /> <br /> FYI - the &quot;official&quot; definition of grimdark at Grimdark Magazine is, &quot;Morally Ambiguous fantasy or science fiction with antiheroes, a corrupt noir world, and no hope of the world changing or getting better. Any victories for morality are fleeting or personal.&quot;<br /> <br /> Examples: A Song of Ice and Fire, The First Law Trilogy, Warhammer 40K, Judge Dredd.<br /> <br /> Noblebright is heroic protagonsits, uplifting morals, and a chance to change the world for the better.<br /> <br /> Example: My Little Pony, Friendship is Magic<br /> <br /> Oddly, I'd avoid using the LOTOR because Tolkien's world is surprisingly cynical and horrible outside of Hobbiton.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T17:10:31-07:00","id":1379950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379938#post1379938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25988_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25988\" data-vbnamecard=\"25988\">Val_Nir</a> I like violence in my games. I just like hearts and romance too.<br /> <br /> Fall of Mexico would be awesome \ud83d\ude0a.</div> </div> </div> </div>Me too! I love to combine these two elements too. That was not a small part of Montreal by Night awesomeness to me, the fact of post-human, monstrous if viewed from human morality POV, beings expressing genuine love and care towards each other.<br /> <br /> By the way, I just recalled a part from BJD on Mexico which combines the two. A letter by a Cam Nosferatu who got his inflitrator coterie caught in the middle of the start of the sabbat civil war just hours after the news of Regent' assasination spread out. All hell breaks loose, they run for their unlives through the most vicious, Masquearade-shattering vampire violence imaginable, shadows wielded as swords and fleshwarped monsters storming through shopping malls; a pack starts pursuing them, kills and dries all but two - the Nosferatu and his lover; when they are almost caught, they kiss and say goodbye to each other when BLAM another pack with crescent moons on their foreheads (some black hand spetsnaz) appears out of the blue and the two packs start tearing each other apart like Camarilla ones aren't even there. <br /> The Nosferatus escaped, struggling to believe their own luck. It was awesome.<br /> <br /> Fall of London will have something like that, too. It has to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T17:16:02-07:00","id":1379952,"title":"","content":"My interpretation of V5 is that it's central theme is a modern day adaptation of the Dark Ages plotline.<br /> <br /> * A modern day Inquisition hunting and destroying Kindred everywhere.<br /> * The corrupt and evil Elders throwing their childer at the Inquisition.<br /> * The Anarchs getting organized and more violent to revolt against their sires.<br /> * The Antediluvians stirring in the background.<br /> * A bunch of Sabbat getting together to destroy the Antediluvians, only to serve their purposes.<br /> <br /> Essentially, I define V5 as &quot;Transylvania Chronicles, 21st Century Edition&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T17:22:40-07:00","id":1379959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379942#post1379942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Back in the original World of Darkness, there was a struggle between &quot;adult content&quot; vs. &quot;for our largely teenage audience of Goth kids and white suburbanites mildly rebelling against their parents that include considerable overlap.&quot; This isn't me making a supposition, it's the reason why Black Dog Games existed. Black Dog Games existed to be the more mature darker lineage and while some were complete fucking disasters (I own one of the few remaining copies of Eternal Hearts that hasn't been burned by sane men), others were dealing with the extreme dark themes and violence that was usually only alluded at.<br /> <br /> <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> 5E is a game that is marketed not at teenagers but at the now-thirty something original audience of the Nineties. The teenagers who have grown up. So was V20 for the most part but this has gone even more so. They've embraced dark topics, violence, and political subjects (sometimes to considerable disaster) while reaffirming the game's social content. It's all Black Dog now.<br /> <br /> So, yes, I feel V5 is a darker more mature take on the World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I wish it was that way, sir. To me, it looks like the opposite. Maybe it's what they imply between the lines hinting at what you can or should play. But honestly, this is far from Black Dog. Imagine any of Black Dog books coming out today. Dark Reflections: Spectres, Book of the Wyrm, Fomori Legion, hell, let's go real tough - Chronicle of the Black Labyrinth.<br /> <br /> The publisher and authors would be impaled at the top of the highest Carpathian peak. Metaphorically speaking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T17:27:42-07:00","id":1379960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379942#post1379942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Back in the original World of Darkness, there was a struggle between &quot;adult content&quot; vs. &quot;for our largely teenage audience of Goth kids and white suburbanites mildly rebelling against their parents that include considerable overlap.&quot; This isn't me making a supposition, it's the reason why Black Dog Games existed. Black Dog Games existed to be the more mature darker lineage and while some were complete fucking disasters (I own one of the few remaining copies of Eternal Hearts that hasn't been burned by sane men), others were dealing with the extreme dark themes and violence that was usually only alluded at.<br /> <br /> <i>Vampire: The Masquerade</i> 5E is a game that is marketed not at teenagers but at the now-thirty something original audience of the Nineties. The teenagers who have grown up. So was V20 for the most part but this has gone even more so. They've embraced dark topics, violence, and political subjects (sometimes to considerable disaster) while reaffirming the game's social content. It's all Black Dog now.<br /> <br /> So, yes, I feel V5 is a darker more mature take on the World of Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Black Dog was um, very edgelordy? to try and use the modern phrasing. Generally came over as trying way too hard. I don't know about how other people mature, but generally that kind of stuff is less appealing when you're not an edgy teenager anymore, so why the hell they'd be trying to i don't know.<br /> <br /> And again, becomes more baffling when the actual product is less dark than the mainline WW. There's far less of a darkness now, and the world has suffered for it...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necroticbinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379940#post1379940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's like saying that someone violating humanity sins (Which are, in effective, 3-4 more tenets, unless you count convictions) is players doing something deliberately and not learning from it each session.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, i find it hard to believe that they are learning nothing about how to maintain their path.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necroticbinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379940#post1379940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To go down to Humanity 1 requires multiple mass murders, to get bbelow humanity 1 well. It requires as it states &quot;Utter perversion or heinous acts&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, you can just do the heinous acts via dominate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necroticbinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379940#post1379940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The easiest tenets to lose are humanist humanity on are humanist. &quot;Don't kill, don't enslave or torture and don't harm the innocent.&quot;. I'd say that characters can learn and still be forced into situations where they will have to kill, harm, or enslave people to protect the masquerade or what they value. This of course doesn't include the problems that can be forced on people based on what convictions they have and if those get violated.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again this says that they have no creativity. Don't kill and don't harm the innocent are easy to avoid, torture, you have to actively decide to do that, and while not being able to blood bond people can be a pain, this edition makes it impossible to do subtly anyway, so not a huge loss.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T17:28:14-07:00","id":1379961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379959#post1379959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I wish it was that way, sir. To me, it looks like the opposite. Maybe it's what they imply between the lines hinting at what you can or should play. But honestly, this is far from Black Dog. Imagine any of Black Dog books coming out today. Dark Reflections: Spectres, Book of the Wyrm, Fomori Legion, hell, let's go real tough - Chronicle of the Black Labyrinth.<br /> <br /> The publisher and authors would be impaled at the top of the highest Carpathian peak. Metaphorically speaking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its basically hard for me to see the previous editions as anything approaching as mature or dark.<br /> <br /> But eye of the beholder.<br /> <br /> I am surprised you think it's less mature, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jaimemalk</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Black Dog was um, very edgelordy? to try and use the modern phrasing. Generally came over as trying way too hard. I don't know about how other people mature, but generally that kind of stuff is less appealing when you're not an edgy teenager anymore, so why the hell they'd be trying to i don't know.<br /> <br /> And again, becomes more baffling when the actual product is less dark than the mainline WW. There's far less of a darkness now, and the world has suffered for it...</div> </div> </div> </div>Since it's easily the darkest edition of Vampire: The Masquerade ever, I'm confused why you think otherwise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T17:38:58-07:00","id":1379967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379961#post1379961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its basically hard for me to see the previous editions as anything approaching as mature or dark.<br /> <br /> But eye of the beholder.<br /> <br /> I am surprised you think it's less mature, though<br /> <br /> Since it's easily the darkest edition of Vampire: The Masquerade ever, I'm confused why you think otherwise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it's because our definitions of dark are different. Many of people here express the same sentiment towards V5, it seems your personal vision of what's mature and what's not differs greatly from the others who played the same game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T17:55:32-07:00","id":1379973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379967#post1379967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe it's because our definitions of dark are different. Many of people here express the same sentiment towards V5, it seems your personal vision of what's mature and what's not differs greatly from the others who played the same game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually asking what you think isn't mature.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T18:02:13-07:00","id":1379977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jamiemalk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379960#post1379960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Black Dog was um, very edgelordy? to try and use the modern phrasing. Generally came over as trying way too hard. I don't know about how other people mature, but generally that kind of stuff is less appealing when you're not an edgy teenager anymore, so why the hell they'd be trying to i don't know.<br /> <br /> And again, becomes more baffling when the actual product is less dark than the mainline WW. There's far less of a darkness now, and the world has suffered for it...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Yes, i find it hard to believe that they are learning nothing about how to maintain their path.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Nope, you can just do the heinous acts via dominate.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Again this says that they have no creativity. Don't kill and don't harm the innocent are easy to avoid, torture, you have to actively decide to do that, and while not being able to blood bond people can be a pain, this edition makes it impossible to do subtly anyway, so not a huge loss.</div> </div> </div> </div>To confirm: &quot;I've gone down to humanity 0 by doing heinous acts&quot; and &quot;You can avoid killing, torturing people and heinous acts&quot;. You are literally contradicting yourself here bub. The new humanity rules are shit because the rules are flexible. But also, the old humanity rules are good because you've broken them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","name":"Necroticbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T18:07:05-07:00","id":1379979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necroticbinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379977#post1379977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To confirm: &quot;I've gone down to humanity 0 by doing heinous acts&quot; and &quot;You can avoid killing, torturing people and heinous acts&quot;. You are literally contradicting yourself here bub. The new humanity rules are shit because the rules are flexible. But also, the old humanity rules are good because you've broken them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Humanity score is not very well designed and could have replaced all the Predator types to more use.<br /> <br /> I think it was just reimagined with the idea of tailoring chronicles to the needs of your game rather than any hard and fast rules. An action-heavy UNDERWORLD game is different to a social game where every human death is a tragedy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T18:18:08-07:00","id":1379983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379973#post1379973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm actually asking what you think isn't mature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, we've been wondering what you think is...<br /> <br /> But, just before i finally go to sleep, and you might want to get you're self control dice ready... Anarchs, the moody grumpy teenagers are the default faction, the Camarilla are evil 1% ers, the sabbat are too dark for this edition, the Setites have decided to franchise religion and become anarchs, Elders were too powerful so all got shooed away, except not really, Humanity is gone, replaced with some of the easiest to avoid breaking tenets i've seen, and it's harder to lose path even if you do, being BFF's with mortals is now encouraged<br /> <br /> These are the simplistic changes that dumb down the setting. These are what i expect to see from a game targeted at really quite sheltered teenagers who haven't even been allowed to go to the goth shop because they might catch the Satanisms.<br /> <br /> I'm exaggerating, slightly, but the setting has regressed massively in terms of maturity, as in actual mature themes as apposed to a film rating, and complexity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T18:24:05-07:00","id":1379985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necroticbinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379977#post1379977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To confirm: &quot;I've gone down to humanity 0 by doing heinous acts&quot; and &quot;You can avoid killing, torturing people and heinous acts&quot;. You are literally contradicting yourself here bub. The new humanity rules are shit because the rules are flexible. But also, the old humanity rules are good because you've broken them.</div> </div> </div> </div>They were good because they weren't flexable, harsh as hell in fact. I wassailed because the character was doing stuff he didn't think was wrong, but was some truely evil acts. One session, five points of path, something that, by my reading is pretty much impossilble in the V5 write up. I don't know why you think i've broken the humanity rules...<br /> <br /> To clarify, i brought up my wassail in counter to your, &quot;can only be dome by multiple mass murders&quot; claim, not that i'd some how twinked anything. Again, lack of creative thinking being displayed...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":1037,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","user":"jamiemalk","date":".  Clarification 04-09-2020, 09:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T18:31:38-07:00","id":1379986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379973#post1379973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm actually asking what you think isn't mature.</div> </div> </div> </div>For now - for now - we have mostly Beast-Hunger-Passion superficial triangle in which the players are forced to wallow. There is no deeper story, there is no questioning of the meaning of unlife and damnation, there are no mind games, complex plots and intrigues coming to fruition after centuries of preparation, no houses of cards which gave you that horrifying, creeping 'cog in the machine'-feel you wanted desperately to break and take back control - it's just your coterie and your personal eating problems. 'The machine', all of them, were removed - threats are somewhere else, Jyhad is a joke, elders suck, Camarilla is in hiding, Sabbat went kamikaze into middle east. you are a neonate with a smartphone and eating habits and the nights are yours. Chessboard is thrown away and pawns are running around and not even aiming at building something bigger than themselves, like Carthians in VtR, they are just busy looking for blood.<br /> <br /> Maybe someone finds the focus on sucking blood and being emotional mature. I do not. I'd say otherwise - this whole lightening of the mood and removal of angst is a feature of modern times and was not done to give a game a mature feel. It's rather a way to attract new, younger audiences and not to scare them away with 'deep dark lore and philosophizing'. Same marketing trick played by Blizz with WoW (not that it was particularly mature but it felt more complex and believable and now it's just a superficial anime of a story), with Warhammer especially with FB-AoS switch, during the last decade. It's not a bad thing, it's just.. different. I don't find it mature, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> Again, I feel like it could change with time and with new books. At least CbN did something good to the story and now we are waiting for the Cults.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T18:33:27-07:00","id":1379987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jamiemalk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379983#post1379983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, we've been wondering what you think is...</div> </div> </div> </div>Serious question but did you miss my answer?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379942#post1379942\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379942#post1379942\"> Is V5 a NobleBright setting? - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379942#post1379942\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379942#post1379942 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I'm making my first V5 character and have been reading into the book and lore. The more I read, the more the setting seems like a NobleBright setting to me. While I have never played VTM until recently, I have been reading up on its lore over the years (mostly the wiki) and did play a little of VTMB. All this time there seems to be a doom and gloom feel to the world setting of VTM. The Kindred faces the final nights (end of the world). While kine are secretly being controlled by various forces including vamps, which are in control of various governments, organizations etc. Basically the whole setting </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T18:37:48-07:00","id":1379988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379987#post1379987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Serious question but did you miss my answer?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379942#post1379942\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...42#post1379942</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously i must have. but i'm not the only one. I've read your article, and the posts here, but you've really not clarified it much beyond &quot;i feel like its darker&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T18:43:53-07:00","id":1379991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jamiemalk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379988#post1379988\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Obviously i must have. but i'm not the only one. I've read your article, and the posts here, but you've really not clarified it much beyond &quot;i feel like its darker&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>But in a more specific reaction, I think that V5 definitely is a more mature game due to a vareity of factors. Reframing the central conflict between the Camarilla and the Anarchs is a nice job of showing a economic as well as socially relevant interaction based upon the elite 1% as well as entrenched capitalist nobility vs. a more poor as well as struggling yet violent majority. The Thin Bloods also get analyzed as a concept of people who are closer to humans than vampires and may have advantages that could allow them to replace humanity while also leaving them vulnerable to the oppressive system they are found in.<br /> <br /> Like MAGE: REVISED the game is very much about reframing the setting to be less about occult mystery and BIG SCARY MONSTERS than more about living in the &quot;real world&quot; as well as interacting with mortals on a regular basis. The existence of Touchstones is a rough one but make sure the player characters are FORCED on some level to not be totally divorced from human society but have at least one mortal friend to remind them that they can't just totally interact with vampires.<br /> <br /> The depiction of the world is also much better with an international global view of things like the Ashirra, South America, Mexico, and other nations with a nod toward V:TM's massive global fanbase versus its original super-America focus. We also get more acknowledgement of the changes to modern society with the rise of the Global Surveilance State using the Second Inquisition as well as the changes necessary to maintain any form of Masquerade.<br /> <br /> The renewed focus on feeding also encourages player characters to think about the people they use for blood as feeding rather than just resource management as well as the increased chance of frenzy as well as taking innocent lives. That's in addition to incorporating so many real life issues into THE ANARCH and THE CAMARILLA. I feel the game has also gotten back to being the dark progressive horror game of 1st Edition.<br /> <br /> It's a bit more vulgar but I feel like its renewed its focus on personal horror and taking place in the &quot;real world.&quot; Mind you, a large part of this is due to Matthew Dawkin's great writing and the Chronicles involved. RUSTED VEINS is probably one of my all-time favorite adventures and is focused on a drug deal gone bad and human trafficking. I also was a huge fan of THE SACRIFICE which is fundamentally a story about how the Sabbat has failed and how butt hurt this made Malenkov. Its resolved not by shooting up the place but by appealing to Malenkov emotionally and playing politics with Sierra.<br /> <br /> So yes, much darker and more mature game. Like 20%.<br /> <br /> I still loved the previous version(s), obviously but it's my 2nd favorite edition.<br /> <br /> CULTS OF THE BLOOD GODS is perhaps the best written example of the darker and more mature game that it's become but CHICAGO BY NIGHT 5E is also wonderfully human in its dark and tragic stories.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-09-2020, 09:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T18:57:41-07:00","id":1379992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wingstorm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting#post1379651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">... So is the setting of V5, as a whole, considered NobleBright?</div> </div> </div> </div>In short, no.<br /> <br /> It is not.<br /> <br /> You are mistaken about either the definition of noblebright, or the more-or-less mechanically mandated pov of V5 player characters.<br /> <br /> Longer explanation... Noblebright is usually seen as one pole of an axis which begins at &quot;grimdark&quot;, and gets more optimistic as it moves toward &quot;noblebright&quot;.<br /> <br /> From the very first result I got when I googled &quot;<a href=\"https://1d4chan.org/wiki/Noblebright\" target=\"_blank\">noblebright</a>&quot;:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>&quot;Why does the third of the three brothers, who shares his food with the old woman in the wood, go on to become king of the country? Why does James Bond manage to disarm the nuclear bomb a few seconds before it goes off rather than, as it were, a few seconds afterwards? Because a universe where that did not happen would be a dark and hostile place. Let there be goblin hordes, let there be terrible environmental threats, let there be giant mutated slugs if you really must, but let there also be hope. It may be a grim, thin hope, an Arthurian sword at sunset, but let us know that we do not live in vain.&quot;</i> \u2013 Sir Terry Pratchett, \u201cLet There Be Dragons\u201d (A Slip of the Keyboard) </div> </div> </div>In V5, your players are not rooting for the humans to win and build a happy world by the end of the story.<br /> <br /> Your players aren't playing James Bond, they are playing the nuclear bomb. Your players' characters are the goblin hordes. Your players' characters are the terrible environmental threats. Your players' characters are (in a few cases, <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Velya_the_Vivisectionist_and_Elaine_Cassidy\" target=\"_blank\">literally</a>) the giant, mutated slugs.<br /> <br /> For that matter, they are the stone excalibur was stuck in, preventing a new king from rising among the Britons.<br /> <br /> If all your players' characters achieve their goals, it is quite likely there is a very long list of humans who live/die in vain, or at least at the whim of the pcs.<br /> <br /> (Of course, it's your game. Golden rule. Run it how you like at your table. Having fun is the first rule. Yadayada. If you want a world where the good guys can win, and the bad guys are likely to lose, take a look at V2 or VRev, especially Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand. It has been criticized by some -not me- as &quot;<a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Vampions\" target=\"_blank\">Vampions</a>&quot;, but is about as close to noblebright as VtM gets. Besides the Aaron Spelling tv show, of course.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11558-nosimplehiway","name":"Nosimplehiway","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11558_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T19:25:50-07:00","id":1379996,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> I agree with you about Vampire Diaries. And Originals.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhatever scares you, I want to tear it apart.\u201d That\u2019s a line from The Originals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T20:06:10-07:00","id":1380007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379996#post1379996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> I agree with you about Vampire Diaries. And Originals.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhatever scares you, I want to tear it apart.\u201d That\u2019s a line from The Originals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Damon killed like 30 people in the first season.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/s