s/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But seriously, the constant hating on V5 is silly especially when the fact is that the vast majority of writers on V5 are the SAME WRITERS FOR PREVIOUS EDITIONS. It's like saying, &quot;That Tim Cain doesn't know shit about Fallout!&quot; There's a general sense of trying to make this a corporate takeover (as if White Wolf wasn't a corporation to begin with) that just doesn't make any sense.<br /> Your signature summarizes it, &quot;V5 is not VT<br /> People may dislike V5 but the complete lack of any desire to engage with the material is getting a little silly. Especially when it's like, &quot;This is objectively sillier than previous games about being fanged monsters brooding in nightclubs.&quot;<br /> M despite the same writers, rules, and endorsement by the creators.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> DnD 4e had the same writers etc as the previous editions, didn't stop it being terrible, and doing horrific damage to the lore of some of the settings, the material I refuse to engage with is the devs taking a huge dump and the lore and settings and telling me the turds are chocolate","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 04-10-2020, 10:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T07:29:02-07:00","id":1380109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380095#post1380095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But seriously, the constant hating on V5 is silly especially when the fact is that the vast majority of writers on V5 are the SAME WRITERS FOR PREVIOUS EDITIONS. It's like saying, &quot;That Tim Cain doesn't know shit about Fallout!&quot; There's a general sense of trying to make this a corporate takeover (as if White Wolf wasn't a corporation to begin with) that just doesn't make any sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this really the case? You got a list of lineups somewhere? Because V5 reads like someone doesn't &quot;Get it&quot;; They see all the bells and whistles but they don't understand the underlying themes and subtext. I'm <i>well aware </i>that they've got a few writers from DAV20 in V5, evidently DAV20 was a stepping stone for the new edition. But do they have any older hands? are newer writers not dominating? <br /> <br /> The only thing that's darker in V5 is that nobody knows what the flying fuck is going on. I guess thin bloods getting powers is the greatest suggestion of a 'time of thin blood' ever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T09:09:38-07:00","id":1380140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380109#post1380109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this really the case? You got a list of lineups somewhere? Because V5 reads like someone doesn't &quot;Get it&quot;; They see all the bells and whistles but they don't understand the underlying themes and subtext. I'm <i>well aware </i>that they've got a few writers from DAV20 in V5, evidently DAV20 was a stepping stone for the new edition. But do they have any older hands? are newer writers not dominating?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is from the corebook.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/VHkHvoE.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Perhaps you recognize a few names.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only thing that's darker in V5 is that nobody knows what the flying fuck is going on. I guess thin bloods getting powers is the greatest suggestion of a 'time of thin blood' ever. </div> </div> </div>For me, the gritty dark street feel is what makes it darker as well as willingness to tackle mature themes of abuse as well as humanity loss. The previous editions all dealt with this but I think V5 does it better.<br /> <br /> I think the Chicago by Night character expansions were the best writing so far as was Cults of the Blood Gods which brought back the mysterious as well as occult nature of the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-10-2020, 12:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T11:11:31-07:00","id":1380160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380085#post1380085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, I'm probably not the person to debate this because I found almost every Path nonsensical and impossible to use in a game, especially if some vampires were on Humanity.<br /> <br /> The take in Cults of the Blood Gods is that Paths are branches off Humanity with bizarre and terrifying rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for confirming. You didn't get a big part of the game and want the current edition to eschew it for some reason going forward. I understand your need to champion the V5 here, and I partially support you in that crusade, I wonder why you also need to dumb down the parts of the game which made it so appealing for so many people for the last two decades, and why you don't understand that the addition of these things would only benefit your beloved V5 with more $, more positive reviews and more people playing it and talking about it.<br /> <br /> I am here in these forums to let the authors who possibly check them from time to time know that there are still fans of old editions who are not complete haters of the new one but would greatly appreciate the end of handholding us as STs and players over the 'object' morality-check subject and the focus solely on feeding/roleplaying passions, in favor of more detached and intricate concepts - concept of going beyond Humanity, for example.<br /> <br /> CTPhipps, please, stop painting anything and anyone willing and wanting to play something else than a street level romantic thug ruminating over his dead girlfriend night after night as a soulless monster in RL who wants to roleplay a supercharged soulless monster. There is - or was - so much more to the game than just the V1 focus on relationships with mortals and desperate attempts of not being a douche in the American Christian morality POV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","user":"Val_Nir","date":". 04-10-2020, 02:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T11:25:43-07:00","id":1380162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FearGrounds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380043#post1380043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cults of the Blood Gods pretty much gives you the tools you need to make the necromancer of your nightmares. No all of the powers, from older versions, are not included in this one book. But more will be released, in time.<br /> <br /> The introduction of &quot;organized religion&quot; pretty much brings back &quot;paths&quot; for everyone who doesn't want to play with human morality. The different cults featured in the book, give you lists of convictions for them, and lets you adapt your play style to whatever it is you are looking for. With the inclusion of the &quot;How to Build Your Own Cult&quot; section, whatever path you miss from previous editions can be remade in V5.<br /> <br /> The re-introduction of bloodlines brings many familiar faces back to the table, and shows me(at least) that the Sabbat is still going to be a force to be feared. Do you have to play Giovanni as heartless soul devouring monsters, no. But the option is still there. Want to play a homicidal Nagaraja....Go right ahead. Is Lamia what you are looking for? They're here too. Just because they are called Hecata, DOES NOT mean that the individual bloodlines have stopped ANY of their goals or ambitions.<br /> <br /> The Lasombra are a part of the Anarch movement... Yeah, ok? Is it really that inconceivable; that the Lasombra would sacrifice a few of their own in order to extend their reach? Let's not forget that the Lasombra are still pulling the strings for the worlds most powerful mortal religion...<br /> <br /> The Ministry, sacrificed a few of their number as well. Why? So that they could join the Camarilla? Not very likely. So that they could destroy it, from the inside out. Now that makes more sense.<br /> <br /> If you want to take everything for face value, it does first appear that the power structures have fallen. But in the dark of the night, the truth will reveal itself. The Sabbat are still here, just not making as much noise. The Camarilla is still here, and crushing the dreams of fledglings nightly. The Anarchs think they are getting ahead, but just may be in for one hell of a rude awakening...<br /> <br /> The hunger dice (Hated by some/Loved by others) give the beast a driving voice in the World of Darkness. All Kindred feel a hunger unlike anything any of us has ever experienced. The simple phrase that we halfheartedly use of &quot;I'm Starving&quot;, for example. How many of us can honestly say that we have went for more than a couple days without food? Most of us can't go an entire day. The average Adult can survive for about a week without food, provided they still have access to water. Dehydration can claim you much, much faster. Kindred cannot eat food. They cannot drink water. Every night of their existence, is an agonizing reminder of that. The only thing that they can do, to at least numb the hunger, is to drink blood. The blood does not actually remove the hunger they feel. It just masks it, for a short time. And the more they force their blood(rouse checks and such) the quicker the hunger returns to them. Just imagine what it would feel like to not eat for a couple of weeks, what might you do to get that pain to go away? Even if only for a night. Then imagine to not eat for a year...<br /> <br /> This world can be as dark as you, the Storyteller, want it to be. The same as every other version of Vampire. Yeah the Meta Plot changes with every edition. So, just use the parts you like, and discard the rest. The lines on a road help you get where you're going, but in no way prevent you from going where you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still cannot commit diablerie without losing humanity<br /> <br /> Still cannot create ghouls without gaining stains<br /> <br /> Still cannot embrance without gaining stains<br /> <br /> Still cannot don't be a babysitter","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T12:07:59-07:00","id":1380170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380084#post1380084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, it's strapping a jet engine to a tricycle and calling it a Tomcat time then, without the Hierarchy of Sins being baked in at a core level to the system, <b>and being utterly rigid and unchangeable between STs and Chronicles</b>, it always will be, which is why the current 'humanity' fails even at being the Via Humanitas.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is the first time I've ever seen someone argue that rigid, inflexible rules that can never be changed, overridden, or interpreted differently by the ST is a <i>good</i> thing. I'm not even sure how that would be enforced. Do you want White Wolf to break into the ST's house and hold them at gunpoint if they interpret Humanity differently?<br /> <br /> The ST's discretion should always override anything in the books, that's how this style of tabletop gaming works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24808,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","user":"Draconis","date":". 04-10-2020, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T12:11:35-07:00","id":1380172,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna be honest with you, I rarely pay attention to credits. Who there is a veteran? I'm gonna guess that most of those people are new hands. <br /> <br /> V5 has lost utterly in political horror. You have far too much choice. <br /> personal horror? well you're in less control over yourself than prior editions and Humanity is 10x level so, whilst losing it is a harder now unless you have a taste of advancement, you're never getting it back. <br /> <br /> The Real horror of V5 is the quality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T12:33:33-07:00","id":1380177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380160#post1380160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks for confirming. You didn't get a big part of the game and want the current edition to eschew it for some reason going forward.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, no, stop. You don't get to gatekeep that my disliking Paths makes me less of a fan after going on and on about how much you hate V5. I've been here since 1995 of gaming and dislike one element. Not cool.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> CTPhipps, please, stop painting anything and anyone willing and wanting to play something else than a street level romantic thug ruminating over his dead girlfriend night after night as a soulless monster in RL who wants to roleplay a supercharged soulless monster. There is - or was - so much more to the game than just the V1 focus on relationships with mortals and desperate attempts of not being a douche in the American Christian morality POV. </div> </div> </div>I'm not trying to take away your playstyle. Nor do I think that playing an unrepentant monster in V:TM is a bad thing in gaming. I have always felt the Paths were very badly written because you have things like, &quot;Suffering an Infidel to Live&quot; and &quot;Failing to Kill a Humane Vampire&quot; in the Heirarchy of Sins that makes the social element very difficult.<br /> <br /> Badly written doesn't mean I don't think that they aren't a good idea.<br /> <br /> I just think that Roads were done a lot better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380172#post1380172\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm gonna be honest with you, I rarely pay attention to credits. Who there is a veteran? I'm gonna guess that most of those people are new hands.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Jason Carl: </b>More or less the creator of Vampire: The Masquerade LARP.<br /> <br /> <b>Mark Rein Hagen: </b>Wrote Vampire: The Masquerade 1st Edition. He is the creator of the game. He also wrote Vampire: The Masquerade: Dark Ages and co-wrote Werewolf.<br /> <br /> <b>Matthew Dawkins: </b>The creative developer of Onyx Path's V:TM line and writer of things like Beckett's Jyhad Diary.<br /> <br /> <b>Kennite Hite: </b>Writer of the Cainite Heresy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-10-2020, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T12:51:43-07:00","id":1380186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380162#post1380162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Still cannot commit diablerie without losing humanity</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that being able to commit diablerie without losing a Path point is stupid. You eat someone's soul. That will fuck you up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Still cannot create ghouls without gaining stains </div> </div> </div>If a tenant is &quot;Never Treat a Mortal as an Equal&quot; then you should absolutely not get a stain.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Still cannot embrance without gaining stains </div> </div> </div>Again, take a tenant that way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Still cannot don't be a babysitter </div> </div> </div>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T13:04:45-07:00","id":1380188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380170#post1380170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this is the first time I've ever seen someone argue that rigid, inflexible rules that can never be changed, overridden, or interpreted differently by the ST is a <i>good</i> thing. I'm not even sure how that would be enforced. Do you want White Wolf to break into the ST's house and hold them at gunpoint if they interpret Humanity differently?<br /> <br /> The ST's discretion should always override anything in the books, that's how this style of tabletop gaming works.</div> </div> </div> </div>So that unless it is declared, in advance as a house rule, I know, without having to ask any more questions, exactly how the Paths work, what the sins are, what any and all rites are etc etc., no 'mother may I' no varying interpretations, the rules being the rules, simple, understandable, fixed and stable. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380186#post1380186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1)I think that being able to commit diablerie without losing a Path point is stupid. You eat someone's soul. That will fuck you up.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 2)If a tenant is &quot;Never Treat a Mortal as an Equal&quot; then you should absolutely not get a stain.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 3)Again, take a tenant that way.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 4)?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) I think anything with the name Humanity should have as it's highest sin, killing for any reason, (i.e 1e humanity got it right) you want to be a killer, or a thief, or anything but a saint, take a path, doesn't mean I am right, and if anything Diablerie should sate the beast and make it quieter, restoring path, if you have the right one. <br /> <br /> 2)Except to have that tenet you now have to babysit an associated mortal<br /> <br /> 3)with brings an added mortal to babysit <br /> <br /> 4) see above comments about touchstones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 04-10-2020, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T13:21:58-07:00","id":1380192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380170#post1380170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this is the first time I've ever seen someone argue that rigid, inflexible rules that can never be changed, overridden, or interpreted differently by the ST is a <i>good</i> thing. I'm not even sure how that would be enforced. Do you want White Wolf to break into the ST's house and hold them at gunpoint if they interpret Humanity differently?<br /> <br /> The ST's discretion should always override anything in the books, that's how this style of tabletop gaming works.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the best things about Humanity was that it was so unreasonable. It didn't care if killing the bad man saved 50 people, you still took the check. It was glorious...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T13:33:08-07:00","id":1380194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jamiemalk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380192#post1380192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One of the best things about Humanity was that it was so unreasonable. It didn't care if killing the bad man saved 50 people, you still took the check. It was glorious...</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I much preferred the way Bloodlines handled it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1) I think anything with the name Humanity should have as it's highest sin, killing for any reason, (i.e 1e humanity got it right) you want to be a killer, or a thief, or anything but a saint, take a path, doesn't mean I am right, and if anything Diablerie should sate the beast and make it quieter, restoring path, if you have the right one. </div> </div> </div>What do you think diablerie is and its role in the game should be is I think a larger question of it, I believe. In my games, I highlight it permanently merges someone else's soul with your own in exchange for power. You no longer are ever going to be the same person you were before. You may suddenly like classical music, have memories of WW2 where you preyed on Slavs, and struggle with disassociative identity disorder if you didn't particularly have an iron will.<br /> <br /> If you are on Humanity and devour, say, someone on the Path of Caine then you ABSOLUTELY know for a fact that said religion is right or suffer some sympathy for it.<br /> <br /> If you are a Path of Blood 9 followers, devouring a vampire on Golconda will forever let you know that you cannot escape human sympathy, love, and redemption.<br /> <br /> The cost for diablerie is that it destroys your sense of self. Your identity. Who you are.<br /> <br /> But the reward is POWER.<br /> <br /> For other games, diablerie may be far less dramatic and is just absorbing some soul juice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T13:41:35-07:00","id":1380196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380188#post1380188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2)Except to have that tenet you now have to babysit an associated mortal<br /> <br /> 3)with brings an added mortal to babysit<br /> <br /> 4) see above comments about touchstones.</div> </div> </div> </div>You do realize that not all mortals you know are Touchstones, right? Unless you have a ridiculous ST not every injury to every mortal you come in contact with risks harm to your Humanity, and if you do then the problem is with the ST and not the system. Moreover, if you think that &quot;having a Ghouled mortal around&quot; is equivalent to babysitting, why are you Ghouling mortals? That's not even relevant to the system, that's just the pros and cons of outsourcing labor to SPCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25972-illithidactivity","name":"IllithidActivity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T13:53:06-07:00","id":1380199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380177#post1380177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm sorry, no, stop.<br /> <br /> You don't get to gatekeep that my disliking Paths makes me less of a fan after going on and on about how much you hate V5. I've been here since 1995 of gaming and dislike one element.<br /> <br /> Not cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please re-read my comments. Never have I said I hate V5. Quite the contrary.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T13:54:18-07:00","id":1380201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380199#post1380199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Please re-read my comments. Never have I said I hate V5. Quite the contrary.</div> </div> </div> </div>My apologies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T14:31:06-07:00","id":1380206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IllithidActivity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380196#post1380196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You do realize that not all mortals you know are Touchstones, right? Unless you have a ridiculous ST not every injury to every mortal you come in contact with risks harm to your Humanity, and if you do then the problem is with the ST and not the system. Moreover, if you think that &quot;having a Ghouled mortal around&quot; is equivalent to babysitting, why are you Ghouling mortals? That's not even relevant to the system, that's just the pros and cons of outsourcing labor to SPCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>About 3, if you have a Tenet &quot;Nurtre Ghouls&quot; as a excuse to don't gain stains ghouling someone (as pipes said) your character now have do babysit ghouls OR gain stains anyway. That would be the same result: be a babysiter or gain a stain","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T14:50:05-07:00","id":1380207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380206#post1380206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> About 3, if you have a Tenet &quot;Nurtre Ghouls&quot; as a excuse to don't gain stains ghouling someone (as pipes said) your character now have do babysit ghouls OR gain stains anyway. That would be the same result: be a babysiter or gain a stain</div> </div> </div> </div>The Tenet that CTPhipps suggested to mitigate Stains from Ghouling was &quot;Never Treat a Mortal as an Equal,&quot; not &quot;Nurture Ghouls.&quot; Never treating a mortal as equal doesn't equate to babysitting mortals. If you DID have the Tenet &quot;Nurture Ghouls&quot; (which is bizarrely specific) then you're better off never making a Ghoul, and that means that's the kind of game the ST is going for. One where mortals are considered precious enough that they shouldn't be put in harm's way, hence using them as slave labor via Ghouling is bad. That's up to the ST.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25972-illithidactivity","name":"IllithidActivity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T15:21:20-07:00","id":1380215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IllithidActivity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380196#post1380196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You do realize that not all mortals you know are Touchstones, right? Unless you have a ridiculous ST not every injury to every mortal you come in contact with risks harm to your Humanity, and if you do then the problem is with the ST and not the system. Moreover, if you think that &quot;having a Ghouled mortal around&quot; is equivalent to babysitting, why are you Ghouling mortals? That's not even relevant to the system, that's just the pros and cons of outsourcing labor to SPCs.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> but every tenet has to have an associated human. So you have to babysit them (and infantilize them, it gets into extreme abusive relationship territory really fast...), or get stains (or loose your Touchstone which destroys the associated Tenet. Nothing outside you should be determining your Path rating. You follow or not, believe or not, that should not depend on 'I can only believe because Steve from accounting hasn't changed the way he acts in the last decade, but if someone or something causes him to change, that will magically reduce my resistance to the beast'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T15:37:41-07:00","id":1380218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380215#post1380215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> but every tenet has to have an associated human. So you have to babysit them (and infantilize them, it gets into extreme abusive relationship territory really fast...), or get stains (or loose your Touchstone which destroys the associated Tenet. Nothing outside you should be determining your Path rating. You follow or not, believe or not, that should not depend on 'I can only believe because Steve from accounting hasn't changed the way he acts in the last decade, but if someone or something causes him to change, that will magically reduce my resistance to the beast'</div> </div> </div> </div>Every conviction has an associated human, not tenant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T15:45:51-07:00","id":1380219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380162#post1380162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Still cannot commit diablerie without losing humanity<br /> <br /> Still cannot create ghouls without gaining stains<br /> <br /> Still cannot embrance without gaining stains<br /> <br /> Still cannot don't be a babysitter</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1 when you take a religion as your convictions, you no longer worry about humanity, as humanity is basically mortal christian faith. If your new religion supports Diablerie, then you will not suffer a loss in your convictions. Just need to make sure that the storyteller is aware that you are not on the humanity &quot;path&quot; anymore.<br /> <br /> 2. Why not? Many of the included religions include ghouls specifically in their congregations, some even ghoul mortals as part of their initiation into the faith. Hence, no stains. They are still treated as lesser than Kindred, but slightly better than mortals.<br /> <br /> 3. Spreading the faith can include recruiting from the mortal herds of followers. Yes there are mixed (Kindred/Kine) faiths represented in this book. So if you are embracing in service of your religion, again, no stains.<br /> <br /> 4. The only babysitting you have to do, is when you make a childe. If you don't want to have to watch out for someone else, then don't embrace anyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26038-feargrounds","name":"FearGrounds","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T15:46:31-07:00","id":1380220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380218#post1380218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Every conviction has an associated human, not tenant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mea culpea, I mixed up the terminology, sorry. Wider point stands however ( also gets me onto half of your characters path choice being dictated by the ST, which isn't great, either Paths or allowed or they aren't, if they are allowed then the Sins are in the book in writing, 1-10, same as always)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T15:49:24-07:00","id":1380222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380220#post1380220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mea culpea, I mixed up the terminology, sorry. Wider point stands however ( also gets me onto half of your characters path choice being dictated by the ST, which isn't great, either Paths or allowed or they aren't, if they are allowed then the Sins are in the book in writing, 1-10, same as always)</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to want to play a game of Vampire the Masquerade that features no internal conflict or moral ambiguity, and expect your Storyteller to be adversarial to your developing personal story. For the former issue I don't know that the genre is necessarily lending itself to the game you want to play, and for the latter I don't think that any system or edition will mitigate that issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25972-illithidactivity","name":"IllithidActivity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T15:55:00-07:00","id":1380223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380140#post1380140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is from the corebook.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/VHkHvoE.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Perhaps you recognize a few names.</div> </div> </div> </div>Everyone there is new except MHR who hadn't written for VtM for decades and did very little actual writing for V5, Kenneth Hite who has written for VtM in the past a few times and Dawkins who came in half way through V20. So half to two thirds of the team was new people...<br /> <br /> Yes, Martin did a bunch of LARPs and worked on the MMO...thats not writing for TTRPGs though. Jason wrote some LARP books, LARP concerns, settings and mechanics are by necessity very different to Tabletop.<br /> <br /> And of course Neil Gaiman is only there on a technicality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","user":"Damian May","date":". 04-10-2020, 07:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may",