-10T16:51:25-07:00","id":1380237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380231#post1380231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's a weird objection to my answer to, &quot;Everyone here has no experience with Vampire: The Masquerade.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Kenneth Hite came up with V5's premise.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The point being that they understand the game, mood, and theme. One may DISAGREE with their choices but the idea they are just hacks put on it is silly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> True. No objection, I was just expanding, I mean looking at KBA its pretty obvious Hite was the driving force behind SI for instance.<br /> <br /> New doesn't mean hacks. There are a bunch of 'new' writers on W5 that are keeping my hopes up that it won't be a total schmozzle and will actually address important issues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T16:54:14-07:00","id":1380238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FearGrounds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380219#post1380219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> 1 when you take a religion as your convictions, you no longer worry about humanity, as humanity is basically mortal christian faith. If your new religion supports Diablerie, then you will not suffer a loss in your convictions. Just need to make sure that the storyteller is aware that you are not on the humanity &amp;quot;path&amp;quot; anymore.<br /> <br /> 2. Why not? Many of the included religions include ghouls specifically in their congregations, some even ghoul mortals as part of their initiation into the faith. Hence, no stains. They are still treated as lesser than Kindred, but slightly better than mortals.<br /> <br /> 3. Spreading the faith can include recruiting from the mortal herds of followers. Yes there are mixed (Kindred/Kine) faiths represented in this book. So if you are embracing in service of your religion, again, no stains.<br /> <br /> 4. The only babysitting you have to do, is when you make a childe. If you don't want to have to watch out for someone else, then don't embrace anyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am talking about the official rules, not about your homebrew.<br /> In v5 rules its very explicit: when you diablerise, you auto lose 1 point of humanity. <br /> <br /> Period.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"r