onyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T17:33:05-07:00","id":1380248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FearGrounds</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380219#post1380219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> 1 when you take a religion as your convictions, you no longer worry about humanity, as humanity is basically mortal christian faith. If your new religion supports Diablerie, then you will not suffer a loss in your convictions. Just need to make sure that the storyteller is aware that you are not on the humanity &amp;quot;path&amp;quot; anymore.<br /> <br /> 2. Why not? Many of the included religions include ghouls specifically in their congregations, some even ghoul mortals as part of their initiation into the faith. Hence, no stains. They are still treated as lesser than Kindred, but slightly better than mortals.<br /> <br /> 3. Spreading the faith can include recruiting from the mortal herds of followers. Yes there are mixed (Kindred/Kine) faiths represented in this book. So if you are embracing in service of your religion, again, no stains.<br /> <br /> 4. The only babysitting you have to do, is when you make a childe. If you don't want to have to watch out for someone else, then don't embrace anyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>About 4, you HAVE TO babysit 1~3 Touchstones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T17:47:00-07:00","id":1380251,"title":"","content":"No. You do not &quot;HAVE TO&quot; babysit touchstones unless you are dealing with a hostile ST. At which point, the theme and mechanics of any game can and will be used against you. Maybe actually argue in good faith Blailton rather than forcing a situation so hostile to proper RPG playing that no system would be good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","name":"Necroticbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T18:13:45-07:00","id":1380256,"title":"","content":"You kinda phrased it awkwardly, but I understand where your going and I agree with you. Basically V5 has nuked the setting. The 2nd Inquisition has basically killed everything off, Elders all mysteriously have gone to the Middle-East, your shoehorned to be a young neonate, they are making Thin-Bloods SOMEHOW relative to the game, killed off the Sabbat, made the most basic faction get to the forefront (Anarchs), etc. <br /> <br /> Its basically a waiting game for the Antediluvians to just wreck everything now. The only point of bringing VTM back from the gutter was as I said many times in other posts- just to move the game forward past the 1990s. Not add in all these mechanics from VTR screwing over the game. Not destroying Sects that have been a staple to the faction dynamics. Not forcing political human biases into Vampires. The main appeal of VTM is roleplaying being a Vampire, one of the monsters. Not overly caring about real world politics despite some overlaps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T18:16:28-07:00","id":1380257,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380256#post1380256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You kinda phrased it awkwardly, but I understand where your going and I agree with you. Basically V5 has nuked the setting. The 2nd Inquisition has basically killed everything off, Elders all mysteriously have gone to the Middle-East, your shoehorned to be a young neonate, they are making Thin-Bloods SOMEHOW relative to the game, killed off the Sabbat, made the most basic faction get to the forefront (Anarchs), etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you read Chicago by Night 5E? I think its very much still V:TM as it's always been. Just with new threats.<br /> <br /> I will say Fall of London seems to be the most apocalyptic and it's deliberately a city set up to be apoclayptic for vampires.<br /> <br /> The Chicago Folios also states the Sabbat is still around in North America, it's just been broken up into competing groups. The Seven Fires is apparently the Midwest version of the Sabbat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-10-2020, 09:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T19:15:18-07:00","id":1380269,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1379691#post1379691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its laughable to think the thousand times over host of proven pawns will in any way be an obstacle to the Antes rather then a Tool. I mean baring some prophetic Last Daughter of Eve McGuffin.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> See I was confused on what was retconned and what wasn't especially after V20 kind of had its own continuity .</div> </div> </div> </div>V20 is not real VTM. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25995-ethryo","name":"Ethryo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T19:29:41-07:00","id":1380271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ethryo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380269#post1380269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> V20 is not real VTM.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> ...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T20:04:37-07:00","id":1380285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necroticbinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380251#post1380251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. You do not &amp;quot;HAVE TO&amp;quot; babysit touchstones unless you are dealing with a hostile ST. At which point, the theme and mechanics of any game can and will be used against you. Maybe actually argue in good faith Blailton rather than forcing a situation so hostile to proper RPG playing that no system would be good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you have to.<br /> <br /> Unless your ST are using house rule, it's mandatory to player character have Touchstone.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And the RPG says the ST must put dilemmas, making the player choose BETWEN Touchstones or have fun. <br /> <br /> If your Touchstone (who is mandatory) get hurt, killed or changed your character get punished by the system to LOSE a attribute (to a point at you cannot make sex anymore, among other consequences).<br /> <br /> So, yes, you have to babysitter a human beign and the ST must threath your touchstone often and thats is a RPG issue, and not a ST issue.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://s6.gifyu.com/images/unnamed4fba800046b5c3ac.png\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://s6.gifyu.com/images/unnamed4fba800046b5c3ac.png\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://s6.gifyu.com/images/unnamed4fba800046b5c3ac.png\" target=\"_blank\"> https://s6.gifyu.com/images/unnamed4fba800046b5c3ac.png </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T20:35:43-07:00","id":1380291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380285#post1380285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, you have to.<br /> <br /> Unless your ST are using house rule, it's mandatory to player character have Touchstone.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And the RPG says the ST must put dilemmas, making the player choose BETWEN Touchstones or have fun.<br /> <br /> If your Touchstone (who is mandatory) get hurt, killed or changed your character get punished by the system to LOSE a attribute (to a point at you cannot make sex anymore, among other consequences).<br /> <br /> So, yes, you have to babysitter a human beign and the ST must threath your touchstone often and thats is a RPG issue, and not a ST issue.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://s6.gifyu.com/images/unnamed4fba800046b5c3ac.png\" target=\"_blank\">https://s6.gifyu.com/images/unnamed4fba800046b5c3ac.png</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, at the risk of being obvious, that's what any good GM (not just of VtM but any narrative RPG) should be doing, rules or no. Player characters should have NPCs that they are emotionally invested in based on their backstories and the developments of the narrative, and then drama is derived from those NPCs either being put in harms way, being threatened or used as collateral, or opposing the PCs ideologically. This is true of all media - your argument that you can't have fun because there exist people who may at some point be in danger is like saying Spider-Man can't swing through NYC because Mary Jane and Aunt May live in the city and he has to babysit them. That's where the game is! You say &quot;you must choose between protecting Touchstones or having fun&quot; but protecting the Touchstone is an element of the fun! That you're meant to want to have a life and be a human being despite having been turned into a monster, and the spiteful people around you want to tear you down and use that against you, so you keep your secrets hidden and threaten anyone who could find out, yadda yadda yadda. That's literally how the game is played!<br /> <br /> Look at Spider-Man actually, I feel like this is a great example of the whole process. Peter Parker had a Touchstone in the form of Gwen Stacy. When Norman Osborne remembers he's the Green Goblin and remembers Spider-Man's identity, he targets Spider-Man's loved ones in order to hurt Spider-Man. Gwen Stacy is accidentally killed by Peter's own hand and he goes into a serious breakdown about it. His descent into furious revenge could be considered a drop in Humanity. Later he grieves and reconnects with Mary Jane, establishing a new Touchstone and regaining that aspect of his Humanity that allows him to love despite the danger it brings. Alternatively you could consider his grieving to be a successful Remorse roll (since he has enough Humanity that he can't then kill the Green Goblin) and connecting with MJ is him transferring his Conviction of &quot;Protect the people you love&quot; from one person to another, as is allowable in the rules.<br /> <br /> That is a textbook story, the only difference in VtM is that the emotional fluctuations have a more literal and physical element as your body can potentially degrade as you lose touch with the things that are important to you. But that's the entire <i>point </i>of Vampire: the Masquerade. That's the crux of gothic horror, the monsters around you and the monster within you. Why on earth are you playing the game if you want to be a superhero with none of the baggage? VtM is all baggage! What does your ideal version of VtM look like? If your optimal play is &quot;never get into trouble and don't make any enemies and don't let anyone harm you&quot; then what does gameplay look like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25972-illithidactivity","name":"IllithidActivity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T20:50:52-07:00","id":1380293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IllithidActivity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380222#post1380222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You seem to want to play a game of Vampire the Masquerade that features no internal conflict or moral ambiguity, and expect your Storyteller to be adversarial to your developing personal story. For the former issue I don't know that the genre is necessarily lending itself to the game you want to play, and for the latter I don't think that any system or edition will mitigate that issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the contrary, I want Path to be as rigid, inflexible and central as it used to be, and for it to not have a forced pet system associated with it. I want Sins, all of them, mapping onto degeneration, that deal with the beast, as you give up little strips of control for an easier life, not this 'my morality is chosen by 3 pets and the ST, it never changes and other people can wassail me by changing the pets behaviour'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T20:51:57-07:00","id":1380294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380238#post1380238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am talking about the official rules, not about your homebrew.<br /> In v5 rules its very explicit: when you diablerise, you auto lose 1 point of humanity. <br /> <br /> Period.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why the Sabbat can't be on Humanity. So how do the Paths work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T21:03:18-07:00","id":1380295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380293#post1380293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the contrary, I want Path to be as rigid, inflexible and central as it used to be, and for it to not have a forced pet system associated with it. I want Sins, all of them, mapping onto degeneration, that deal with the beast, as you give up little strips of control for an easier life, not this 'my morality is chosen by 3 pets and the ST, it never changes and other people can wassail me by changing the pets behaviour'</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to play a character that chooses to be a degenerate monster because it's convenient then...kill your Touchstones the moment they become inconvenient to you? Break Chronicle Tenets when they're inconvenient? Play the character and personality that you want to play regardless of the mechanical effects of having that personality? There's literally nothing stopping you except the eventual slide into unplayable degeneracy, which you've said is your eventual goal.<br /> <br /> Also &quot;chosen by 3 pets and the ST,&quot; how reductive. First of all, shocker, <i>you </i>design those so-called pets and the moral code associated with them. You want to be a ruthless dictator? Make your Touchstone the current Prince's Ghoul retainer and the Conviction associated with it be &quot;I'll betray the human race if I come out on top.&quot; All of a sudden anything inhumane you do gives you fewer Stains if it was to a power-hungry end. Secondly, you keep referring to the ST as though they're an adversary who's trying to &quot;getcha&quot; at every turn. Did you forget that this person is presumably a friend of yours and you're playing a collaborative imagination game together, and you get to discuss at the beginning of the chronicle what you want that game to be about? If you're interested in a bloodthirsty, power-hungry, sinful game then &quot;Always grab as much as you can take&quot; could be a Chronicle Tenet and any vampire in the game could be penalized for choosing to be altruistic or merciful.<br /> <br /> Everything you could want is presented to you is a customizable format, but because it doesn't have the name you like and it requires you to think just a little more about your character's motivations you've decided you don't like it. Oh, and of course because hating on V5 is the trendy thing to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25972-illithidactivity","name":"IllithidActivity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T21:12:19-07:00","id":1380297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IllithidActivity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380291#post1380291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, at the risk of being obvious, that's what any good GM (not just of VtM but any narrative RPG) should be doing, rules or no. Player characters should have NPCs that they are emotionally invested in based on their backstories and the developments of the narrative, and then drama is derived from those NPCs either being put in harms way, being threatened or used as collateral, or opposing the PCs ideologically. This is true of all media - your argument that you can't have fun because there exist people who may at some point be in danger is like saying Spider-Man can't swing through NYC because Mary Jane and Aunt May live in the city and he has to babysit them. That's where the game is! You say &quot;you must choose between protecting Touchstones or having fun&quot; but protecting the Touchstone is an element of the fun! That you're meant to want to have a life and be a human being despite having been turned into a monster, and the spiteful people around you want to tear you down and use that against you, so you keep your secrets hidden and threaten anyone who could find out, yadda yadda yadda. That's literally how the game is played!<br /> <br /> Look at Spider-Man actually, I feel like this is a great example of the whole process. Peter Parker had a Touchstone in the form of Gwen Stacy. When Norman Osborne remembers he's the Green Goblin and remembers Spider-Man's identity, he targets Spider-Man's loved ones in order to hurt Spider-Man. Gwen Stacy is accidentally killed by Peter's own hand and he goes into a serious breakdown about it. His descent into furious revenge could be considered a drop in Humanity. Later he grieves and reconnects with Mary Jane, establishing a new Touchstone and regaining that aspect of his Humanity that allows him to love despite the danger it brings. Alternatively you could consider his grieving to be a successful Remorse roll (since he has enough Humanity that he can't then kill the Green Goblin) and connecting with MJ is him transferring his Conviction of &quot;Protect the people you love&quot; from one person to another, as is allowable in the rules.<br /> <br /> That is a textbook story, the only difference in VtM is that the emotional fluctuations have a more literal and physical element as your body can potentially degrade as you lose touch with the things that are important to you. But that's the entire <i>point </i>of Vampire: the Masquerade. That's the crux of gothic horror, the monsters around you and the monster within you. Why on earth are you playing the game if you want to be a superhero with none of the baggage? VtM is all baggage! What does your ideal version of VtM look like? If your optimal play is &quot;never get into trouble and don't make any enemies and don't let anyone harm you&quot; then what does gameplay look like?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires are not Spiderman, they are not human, and they only care about humans as food, experimental subjects or playthings. Gameplay is about Pack, Path and Sect, and the unending war against the Anarchs and Camarilla. All of that is gone, for edgelording look at me fanged ISIS and pedophile gang bullshittery. (in case it isn't clear, I do not believe the frantic spin about the playtest, the hiring decisions and the politics)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 04-11-2020, 12:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T21:17:48-07:00","id":1380298,"title":"","content":"&quot;Make your Touchstone the current Prince's Ghoul retainer&quot;<br /> <br /> As per RAW Touchstones must be human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T21:26:16-07:00","id":1380300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380297#post1380297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Vampires are not Spiderman, they are not human, and they only care about humans as food, experimental subjects or playthings. Gameplay is about Pack, Path and Sect, and the unending war against the Anarchs and Camarilla. All of that is gone, for edgelording look at me fanged ISIS and pedophile gang bullshittery. (in case it isn't clear, I do not believe the frantic spin about the playtest, the hiring decisions and the politics)</div> </div> </div> </div>A vampire wakes up from their Embrace as a slavering idiot? You may well be right that deep down they are fundamentally incapable of loving, but the point of the narrative is to experience how that fundamental lack of what makes a person a person affects them as they try to pretend that they still are one. I feel like you're coming at this with a Warhammer approach. VtM isn't exactly praised for its combat system, so if you're looking for a combat-heavy game things are bound to break down. Still, nothing about V5 denies you the ability to play the Wight you want to be. Like I said, kill your Touchstones day one. Do them all in one session and you may not even lose Humanity, with a lucky roll!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380298#post1380298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Make your Touchstone the current Prince's Ghoul retainer&quot;<br /> <br /> As per RAW Touchstones must be human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghouls are human. They are augmented humans, but human nonetheless. On page 147 it even gives an example of a hypothetical PC making their Ghoul their Touchstone.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25972-illithidactivity","name":"IllithidActivity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T21:28:46-07:00","id":1380301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380298#post1380298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Make your Touchstone the current Prince's Ghoul retainer&quot;<br /> <br /> As per RAW Touchstones must be human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghouls are humans.<br /> <br /> Did you not know they were the most common Touchstone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T21:30:36-07:00","id":1380302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IllithidActivity</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380300#post1380300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A vampire wakes up from their Embrace as a slavering idiot? You may well be right that deep down they are fundamentally incapable of loving, but the point of the narrative is to experience how that fundamental lack of what makes a person a person affects them as they try to pretend that they still are one. I feel like you're coming at this with a Warhammer approach. VtM isn't exactly praised for its combat system, so if you're looking for a combat-heavy game things are bound to break down. Still, nothing about V5 denies you the ability to play the Wight you want to be. Like I said, kill your Touchstones day one. Do them all in one session and you may not even lose Humanity, with a lucky roll!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Ghouls are human. They are augmented humans, but human nonetheless. On page 147 it even gives an example of a hypothetical PC making their Ghoul their Touchstone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you actually reading my replies? Because you aren't actually addressing anything I have said. I never mentioned playing a Wight, I mentioned PATH you know the core concept of the previous editions of the game, from 2e onwards,..... I am describing the Sabbat, and the part of the Cam and independent clans that are on Paths. That deeply personal moral code that defines the struggle against the beast as the quintessential internal war of intellect Vs animal, a conflict not defined by pets, or by lying about being human in anyway, but by will and ideology Vs madness. A conflict not defined by externally imposed tenets, or forced morality pets, but by action, by hierarchy of sins and by personal conviction<br /> <br /> In short I want Honorable Accord. Or Night, or Power and the Inner Voice, not Humanity","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 04-11-2020, 12:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T21:34:01-07:00","id":1380303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380301#post1380301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ghouls are humans.<br /> <br /> Did you not know they were the most common Touchstone?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Isn't ghouling your Touchstone altering it? Since when are people that subsist on vampire blood and punch through steel human? How does an immortal slave addicted to your blood help you ' stay human'?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T21:41:28-07:00","id":1380304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380301#post1380301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ghouls are humans.<br /> <br /> Did you not know they were the most common Touchstone?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think we must have binned that as not making sense early on during playtesting and just never gone back over it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T21:56:39-07:00","id":1380307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380304#post1380304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think we must have binned that as not making sense early on during playtesting and just never gone back over it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, ghouls are the ultimate Touchstones.<br /> <br /> Forced to love you and property!<br /> <br /> Touchstones are a way to make Kindred feel better about themselves by using a human to feel more close to humanity but, in the end, their relationship is parasitic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#cus