book/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T23:40:09-07:00","id":1380327,"title":"","content":"This whole Touchstone thing is just nonsense.. It only works for Wraith: The Oblivion in the form of &quot;Fetters&quot; like I said before. I still don't even know why they ever implemented Touchstones at all into VTM. Its one of the most worst features they put in from VTR.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-10T23:46:05-07:00","id":1380329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380326#post1380326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Presumably a Chronicle Tenant would be, &quot;Betraying the Sabbat&quot; or &quot;Betraying your Pack&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which wouldn't work for Power and the Inner Voice, they will not 'Submit to the Error of Others' and must 'Strive for control by all means, dominate the world and bend it to your will'. If that means throwing the Pack under the bus, or even the local Arch-Bishop, they must do so. (Or for several other paths actually, Self-Focus, Cathari, Night..yea probably could find more)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T00:13:54-07:00","id":1380330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380325#post1380325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> but you will still be on Humanity. that is the disconnect, until, RAW I can remove that phrase from the character sheet, everything else is a ha;f measure. Also PAths go down to at least 6 points, usually more, so you would need that many Convictions, and Touchstones to go with them, because the point of a Paths game is not everyone is on the same one, so Chronicle Tenets would not be helpful to Paths, no Tenet could cover both Power and the Inner Voice and Honorable Accord for instance, they fundamentally don't view the world the same way, and that division is part of what makes the Sabbat so interesting.<br /> <br /> <br /> Actually on topic: Nope, V5 is not Noblebright, I find it less dark and shallower than previous editions, with more obvious 'aren't we shocking' edgelording touches thrown in, (or rather they are more concentrated and earlier).</div> </div> </div> </div>You'll note: I didn't say the Tenet would cover the path. Because the tenets aren't supposed to cover the path. The convictions would cover the path. Just because paths HAD 10 different sins does not mean they HAVE to have 10 different sins to cover the ethical and fundamental understanding of a path. Path of Honorable Accord. Again for example: Chivalry is my code (Or Sabbat Chivarly or whatever) Or, if you want to break it down into three things. My word is my bond. Know your station. Bravery above all. Or if your character is focused more on the duty to their sect side, replace one with &quot;My duties are my life.&quot;. With these convictions, you would be mitigating the stains from almost any action covered by any tenet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","name":"Necroticbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T00:45:51-07:00","id":1380332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necroticbinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380330#post1380330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You'll note: I didn't say the Tenet would cover the path. Because the tenets aren't supposed to cover the path. The convictions would cover the path. Just because paths HAD 10 different sins does not mean they HAVE to have 10 different sins to cover the ethical and fundamental understanding of a path. Path of Honorable Accord. Again for example: Chivalry is my code (Or Sabbat Chivarly or whatever) Or, if you want to break it down into three things. My word is my bond. Know your station. Bravery above all. Or if your character is focused more on the duty to their sect side, replace one with &quot;My duties are my life.&quot;. With these convictions, you would be mitigating the stains from almost any action covered by any tenet.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Nope, sorry, the fewest Honorable Accord breaks down to, and remains recognisable is 7. I just tried. But you miss the point: I WANT THE PATHS...all 10 sins, all of the Ethics, the PATHS, just because they chose to have the utterly sickening, disgusting, feces soaked perverted failure of the 3 convictions humanity, doesn't mean the paths should be defiled and mutilated in the same way. I am sorry, I tried, for pages to make it clear, but apparently 'I want the paths' wasn't clear enough, so maybe the visceral disgust and hatred I feel for the touchstones, convictions and hunger system will make it clear, they are utterly and totally repugnant, morally and ethically without worth. beyond use or saving, and probably the worse mechanics I have seen in any RPG.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25011,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","user":"Taggie","date":". 04-11-2020, 03:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T01:19:06-07:00","id":1380337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380177#post1380177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jason Carl: </b>More or less the creator of Vampire: The Masquerade LARP.<br /> <br /> <b>Mark Rein Hagen: </b>Wrote Vampire: The Masquerade 1st Edition. He is the creator of the game. He also wrote Vampire: The Masquerade: Dark Ages and co-wrote Werewolf.<br /> <br /> <b>Matthew Dawkins: </b>The creative developer of Onyx Path's V:TM line and writer of things like Beckett's Jyhad Diary.<br /> <br /> <b>Kennite Hite: </b>Writer of the Cainite Heresy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Larp should not influence a pen and paper game. LARP offers a system of comprimises so that a bunch of amatuer actors can approach playing the game in dress up, it should never be a shackle for the imagination of pen and paper players. V5 obviously has LARP in mind for it's pen and paper rules: The powers are more LARP friendly, the game encourages players to be nicer.... LARP has done the game only a diservice. That all said... I don't see this name in the list you shared previously.<br /> <br /> I've definetly liked MD's stuff in the past. The man had a standout performance in LotB (Largely because everything else in that book was variably bad). But I don't think he stands at the top, nor do I think his influence on this book was so huge. As for KH; The Cainite Heresy was a servicable book, doesn't stick out in my memory as one of my favourites. Does he do anything else?<br /> <br /> Now, MRH<br /> The dude has a supporting roll. He's not a big writer here. Maybe a paragraph of his was squeezed in.<br /> <br /> Are any of the core writers actually old hands? Are you missing a few? It seems at least Half the Writers are new, All the editors are either new or they were given a credit just to say the book had an editor because clearly, even if you liked it, you must admit the corebook needed some additional editing, and I can only imagine what kind of horrific state it started with if these three people actually did some of their job. Maybe the Old hands wrote something good and were powerless to have it added in due to this tribunal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T04:35:18-07:00","id":1380357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380337#post1380337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Larp should not influence a pen and paper game. LARP offers a system of comprimises so that a bunch of amatuer actors can approach playing the game in dress up, it should never be a shackle for the imagination of pen and paper players. V5 obviously has LARP in mind for it's pen and paper rules: The powers are more LARP friendly, the game encourages players to be nicer.... LARP has done the game only a diservice. That all said... I don't see this name in the list you shared previously.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no proof, but I feel like Carl had the most influence on V5's design,<br /> I read the MET books (the LARP books), and they are very similar to V5:<br /> <br /> - Requiem inspired rules and feel<br /> - sabbat made weaker<br /> - sabbat shifting their attention away from the cam (though instead of going to the middle east, they just decided to go after the independant clans...)<br /> - anarchs made into winners<br /> - plus MET was the first to introduce the second inquisition (though it wasn't called that in the book, iirc it was a hunter onslaught which broke the sabbat...just like V5)<br /> <br /> he's not the only one,<br /> the other guy with the long black hair (forgot his name, think he was the director of white wolf or lead storyteller or something) was a big LARP enthusiast and fond of VtM 1st ed (if I'm not mistaken)<br /> <br /> finally, Dawkins is also a 1st ed fan, and an Anarch fan (he admitted it back then in one of his videos),<br /> he was fond of putting every clan (setites his favorite, lasombra, harbingers etc...) in the Cam<br /> <br /> so...yeah, I don't think V5 is the work of new blood, it definitely lines up with veterans' vision","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 04-11-2020, 08:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T05:41:04-07:00","id":1380365,"title":"","content":"Most of those writers look new to me, though I must admit i'm entirely basing this off the fact that at least half the people in the credits don't have the names of anglophone men, which wasn't the case in 1e.<br /> <br /> Yes, I remember ME telling everyone about how great LARP is. I remember when they first released the nuWoD webite the godamn Werewolves had suggestions for day jobs. Clearly V5's creators have Larp in mind equal to or more than Tabletop.<br /> <br /> This very loose interpretation of 'old blood' seems to be a minority. And quite honestly the book reads like nobody fucking knows what vampire is about. It feels like someone who writes fanfiction as a hobby played at someone's heavily houserulled table once and thought &quot;How can I tailor this to my preferences&quot; before shitting out V5. We've got a noblebright setting that's no longer a dark reflection of our reality, we've narrowed the horror onto focusing on a persecuted minority with mental illnesses (The Beast) and have completely destroyed the political horror by greatly relaxing the control or standards of groups like the Cam or Clan Tremere...<br /> <br /> If 1e was Predator, Fallout 1, Halo 1, Alien, The LoTR Books, V5 is The Predator, Fallout 4, Halo 5, Prometheus, The Hobbit movies. It's not a faithful product despite all claims. For the most part it's not a good product. The people involve mostly either have no idea what made 1e work or they do but wanted to do their own thing in spite of it. V5's horror is just about being different, not about being a monster participating in a struggle under near insurmountable oppression. If V5 really had old hands behind it, why can't I see a spec of influence? Why are fundamental pillars of this series inverted? Maybe they've gone Ridley Scott on us, but I'm more inclined to believe that they had no real input, at least where it counts. You know, near the end of the book I really loved the sections about Graffiti and fuedal city structure, but they're inconsequential when considering the huge sweeping changes everywhere else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T06:11:45-07:00","id":1380368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380365#post1380365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This very loose interpretation of 'old blood' seems to be a minority. And quite honestly the book reads like nobody fucking knows what vampire is about.</div> </div> </div> </div>no they definitely do, they know all about vampire and its different iterations,<br /> some of them like some iterations over others,<br /> and some even hate the iterations they themselves wrote (like the author of revised, who happens to be the same guy who did Requiem lmao, so I imagine he might've done the same with V5)<br /> <br /> so yeah, I don't know why you're so hung up on proving that it's the new blood, but really it's the old blood<br /> <br /> maybe they got bored of the old stuff, maybe they want the old days back, maybe they're not satisfied with their previous stuff, have some regrets, are fond of LARP, or just liked Requiem better...I don't know,<br /> but I'm pretty sure it's the old guys doing it<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If 1e was Predator, Fallout 1, Halo 1, Alien, The LoTR Books, V5 is The Predator, Fallout 4, Halo 5, Prometheus, The Hobbit movies. </div> </div> </div>a better comparison would be star wars prequels,<br /> same ol' dude running the show taking an unexpected direction","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 04-11-2020, 09:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T11:23:12-07:00","id":1380425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380337#post1380337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Larp should not influence a pen and paper game. LARP offers a system of compromises so that a bunch of amatuer actors can approach playing the game in dress up, it should never be a shackle for the imagination of pen and paper players. V5 obviously has LARP in mind for it's pen and paper rules: The powers are more LARP friendly, the game encourages players to be nicer.... LARP has done the game only a diservice. That all said... I don't see this name in the list you shared previously.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're arguing that Live Action Roleplay is not REAL gaming. That is ****ing silly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380365#post1380365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most of those writers look new to me, though I must admit i'm entirely basing this off the fact that at least half the people in the credits don't have the names of anglophone men, which wasn't the case in 1e.</div> </div> </div> </div>So now ALL of the writers have to be old guys even though one of the writers who defends it is the guy who made the game. You know, fine, you hate it. That's your perogitive. I just find the claim, &quot;They don't understand the REAL Vampire: The Masquerade&quot; hard to parse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-11-2020, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T12:03:58-07:00","id":1380439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380332#post1380332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope, sorry, the fewest Honorable Accord breaks down to, and remains recognisable is 7. I just tried. But you miss the point: I WANT THE PATHS...all 10 sins, all of the Ethics, the PATHS, just because they chose to have the utterly sickening, disgusting, feces soaked perverted failure of the 3 convictions humanity, doesn't mean the paths should be defiled and mutilated in the same way. I am sorry, I tried, for pages to make it clear, but apparently 'I want the paths' wasn't clear enough, so maybe the visceral disgust and hatred I feel for the touchstones, convictions and hunger system will make it clear, they are utterly and totally repugnant, morally and ethically without worth. beyond use or saving, and probably the worse mechanics I have seen in any RPG.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll preface this by saying I honestly don't like V5's approach to touchstones. I think &quot;some external thing that helps ground you in your Path&quot; is a good idea, but it should not be limited to a single living human, and it shouldn't be mandatory (especially since we've now seen Touchstoneless NPCs). At least one of the writers has mentioned the Sabbat using their Ritae in place of human touchstones, which I think would help significantly; I hope we get rules for that at some point. Or, say, a Tzimisce Voivode anchored to their ancestral domain, or things like that. That would make more sense to me.<br /> <br /> But, &quot;follow all the tenets of [insert religion here]&quot; is listed as a viable Conviction in the corebook. So, take &quot;don't do anything at a level lower than your current Humanity on the Path of Blood as presented in the V20 book&quot;. Or, less ridiculously, write it on your sheet as &quot;follow the laws of Haqim above all else&quot;, and talk with your ST about how you interpret that.<br /> <br /> Personally, I like the idea that even someone at Path of Blood 1 should care about breaking their word of honor to another faithful follower of Haqim (a level 9 sin); it shouldn't make them Wassail, but it should be something they care about, not just &quot;eh I'm at Path 8, it no longer affects me&quot;. And the Stains system does accomplish that, once you get your ST to allow a Touchstone that lines up with the Path of Blood (which probably involves houserules). If you get down to one dot of Humanity (or Path), the single stain from breaking your word to another follower won't have much of any impact. But, say, betraying your allies to hunters for personal gain should give you quite a lot of Stains, enough that they'll have an impact on you no matter how far you've dropped, because you've gone against one of the fundamental principles that grounds you against the Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T12:12:04-07:00","id":1380440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380337#post1380337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Larp should not influence a pen and paper game. LARP offers a system of comprimises so that a bunch of amatuer actors can approach playing the game in dress up, it should never be a shackle for the imagination of pen and paper players. <b>V5 obviously has LARP in mind for it's pen and paper rules</b>: The powers are more LARP friendly, the game encourages players to be nicer.... LARP has done the game only a diservice.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a longtime LARP player and ST, I have to disagree with this. LARP has always used a fundamentally different resolution mechanic from tabletop, with no d10s involved. But now Hunger is fundamentally linked to the dice system, so a V5 LARP will need to either switch to dice or completely overhaul Hunger (or, most likely, just use the blood pool from earlier editions, which is nice and easy to track: give players tokens to represent their blood points, hand them over to the ST when you spend).<br /> <br /> Similarly, I like a lot of V5's changes to disciplines, like Celerity no longer giving extra actions. But from a LARP perspective, &quot;you can move 50 feet before attacking&quot; is significantly more of a headache for the ST than &quot;you get an extra action at the end of the round&quot;, since it increases the scale of combat quite a lot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T12:29:06-07:00","id":1380443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380440#post1380440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As a longtime LARP player and ST, I have to disagree with this. LARP has always used a fundamentally different resolution mechanic from tabletop, with no d10s involved. But now Hunger is fundamentally linked to the dice system, so a V5 LARP will need to either switch to dice or completely overhaul Hunger (or, most likely, just use the blood pool from earlier editions, which is nice and easy to track: give players tokens to represent their blood points, hand them over to the ST when you spend).<br /> <br /> Similarly, I like a lot of V5's changes to disciplines, like Celerity no longer giving extra actions. But from a LARP perspective, &quot;you can move 50 feet before attacking&quot; is significantly more of a headache for the ST than &quot;you get an extra action at the end of the round&quot;, since it increases the scale of combat quite a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just attach a hunger mechanic to whatever resolution you already use, like a tie in rock paper sissors is a hunger, or a bigger difference than 3 in random card draws, pretty easy to do. Even if they're by themselves a coinflip is a quick and easy way to do it...<br /> <br /> Your larp must be less involved than the one i used to do, 50 feet of movement is less than old celerity 2 would have given you...<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T12:34:13-07:00","id":1380445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380439#post1380439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll preface this by saying I honestly don't like V5's approach to touchstones. I think &amp;quot;some external thing that helps ground you in your Path&amp;quot; is a good idea, but it should not be limited to a single living human, and it shouldn't be mandatory (especially since we've now seen Touchstoneless NPCs). At least one of the writers has mentioned the Sabbat using their Ritae in place of human touchstones, which I think would help significantly; I hope we get rules for that at some point. Or, say, a Tzimisce Voivode anchored to their ancestral domain, or things like that. That would make more sense to me.<br /> <br /> But, &amp;quot;follow all the tenets of [insert religion here]&amp;quot; is listed as a viable Conviction in the corebook. So, take &amp;quot;don't do anything at a level lower than your current Humanity on the Path of Blood as presented in the V20 book&amp;quot;. Or, less ridiculously, write it on your sheet as &amp;quot;follow the laws of Haqim above all else&amp;quot;, and talk with your ST about how you interpret that.<br /> <br /> Personally, I like the idea that even someone at Path of Blood 1 should care about breaking their word of honor to another faithful follower of Haqim (a level 9 sin); it shouldn't make them Wassail, but it should be something they care about, not just &amp;quot;eh I'm at Path 8, it no longer affects me&amp;quot;. And the Stains system does accomplish that, once you get your ST to allow a Touchstone that lines up with the Path of Blood (which probably involves houserules). If you get down to one dot of Humanity (or Path), the single stain from breaking your word to another follower won't have much of any impact. But, say, betraying your allies to hunters for personal gain should give you quite a lot of Stains, enough that they'll have an impact on you no matter how far you've dropped, because you've gone against one of the fundamental principles that grounds you against the Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>BUT YOU STILL LOSE A POINT OF HUMANITY (PATH, IF USING YOUR &quot;don't do anything at a level lower than your current Humanity on the Path of Blood as presented in the V20 book&quot; Conviction) WHEN COMMIT DIABLERIE!!!!!<br /> <br /> A FOLLOWER OF PATH OF BLOOD<br /> <br /> LOSING PATH RATING<br /> <br /> FOR COMMITING <br /> <br /> DIABLERIE<br /> <br /> !!!!<br /> <br /> BUY HUMANITY POINTS IS ALMOST IMPOSSIBLE/IMPOSSIBLE <br /> <br /> IT MEANS <br /> <br /> ANY BANU HAQUIN PLAYER CHARACTER HAVE 100% CHANCE TO BECAME WIGHT AFTER 6~8 DIABLERIES (PROB. WAY LESS BECAUSE YOU CAN LOSE MORE THAN 01 HUMANITY POINT TO EACH DIABLERIE AND THE MATH IS AGAINST YOU LOWER YOU HUMANITY ARE)!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T12:46:45-07:00","id":1380448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380425#post1380425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So now ALL of the writers have to be old guys even though one of the writers who defends it is the guy who made the game. You know, fine, you hate it. That's your perogitive. I just find the claim, &quot;They don't understand the REAL Vampire: The Masquerade&quot; hard to parse.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you need to strawman to make an argument, maybe you aught to rethink your view here? The Vast majority of the team aren't old hands. The writing quality of V5 is <i>bad </i>with a few good bits, not Good with a few bad bits. The editing is a joke. Even if you were right, say, three quaters of the team and all the people in important rolls were the original masterminds or had written great works like <i>midnight seige</i> or the Thaumaturgy trilogy, the issue is that even the most optimistic reader will find the writing needs a bit of work. Ridley Scot has made classics and disasters, Cathleen Kenedy has had a distinguished career, and history is filled with pretty good kings who lost the plot when they got older. <br /> <br /> Now, Onto LARP <br /> <br /> If you want to play dress up and run around a modern ruin, more power to you. I'd play airsoft if I could afford it. However, Larp has a metric fuckton of stuff you can't do. It's not just no-touching rules, there's just stuff you can't do. You can't break down walls, you can't jump a few stories, You can't subtly dominate someone over a long period of time because that's mean and they're likely to follow your command as if it were an obligation rather than as if they were compelled to do it. I Suspect this is a big reason why V5 has stomped dominate into the ground. You can't have five retainers because there aren't enough locals so your retainer dots reflect the quality of one guy, <i>you can't have five appearance because just look at you</i>. When you start designing an unlimited pen'n paper game with larp limitations in mind, you're dragging it down. And you can't be too mean in LARP because the character and player are closer in this matter, so the setting is brighter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T13:00:16-07:00","id":1380452,"title":"","content":"Exactly. Having guys who specialized in only LARP writing up V5 is probably what broke VTM tbh. Where are the main writers from before?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 04-11-2020, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T13:15:52-07:00","id":1380458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380448#post1380448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you need to strawman to make an argument, maybe you aught to rethink your view here?</div> </div> </div> </div>Your argument is wrong and you repeating it doesn't make it any better. You said that no one was involved who was an old hand and then I shared a bunch of veteran writers name, only now you're saying that because they wrote LARP they don't count. That's not so much moving the goal posts as insisting they don't exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a>