ser":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T11:55:32-07:00","id":1380722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379651-is-v5-a-noblebright-setting?p=1380458#post1380458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your argument is wrong and you repeating it doesn't make it any better. You said that no one was involved who was an old hand and then I shared a bunch of veteran writers name, only now you're saying that because they wrote LARP they don't count. That's not so much moving the goal posts as insisting they don't exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>So technically yes, some old hands have been there. But I've already thrown out this argument: Old hands are in the minority. They're between 1 and 3/5 main writers depending on definition (leaning towards the lower numbers). A couple of auxileries, and none of the editing staff. You gave three names (You gave four but one wasn't actually on the list) ; A guy who wrote a book I can't remember much about, A fan-turned writer who came in during the time of onyx path, and some other dude. As much as I remember MD for writing the only good parts of LotB, this isn't really the greatest lot of names you've given us. ]<br /> <br /> My argument, at this point, is not that 'there are no old hands' (Cause I can't refute that you've got at least one) but that the old hands have had no influence on the product. I'm repeating myself here; but as great as the fuedal structures and grafiti sections were, the important changes to the metaplot and metaphysics are what count, and what we have there is either no imput with old writers, or a case of Ridley Scott. <br /> <br /> The discipline changes screw with established metaphysics. <br /> The social changes screw with the very themes of the world of darkness, and they also don't seem reasonable. They're not True, if we take the hermetic viewpoint, because vampire society is no longer a microcosm of which to look at the macrocosm. They don't ring true because they're not based in an objective reality any more. They're also extremely contrived and handwaved... But they certainly aren't a microcosm of the rest of the world like every other edition of vampire has given us. <br /> Certain characters have had changes and, well, they're out of character. Nuff said. <br /> <br /> If you imagine VTM as A song of Ice and Fire, V5 is Game of thrones at the fifth season and beyond where the original writer might have left a few bullet points but the showrunners wanna do their own thing (Honestly i started having big problems with certain threads at season three, it was five where I couldn't watch it anymore)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}